,"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Efren707/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Efren707/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Efren707/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Efren707","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Efren707/toptrader/commits/d964e0e8b84e5aceff008d5f6bef21f4ebc9c8b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T03:33:06Z","email":"53492872+Efren707@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Efren707"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T03:33:06Z","email":"53492872+Efren707@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Efren707"},"message":"fix: drop leading dot from CSRF cookie domain (invalid per RFC 6265)\n\nThe .toptrader.dev value crashed the live app on every request: Tomcat''s\nRFC6265CookieProcessor rejects a leading-dot Domain attribute (legacy\nRFC 2109 syntax, dropped in RFC 6265 - a bare \"toptrader.dev\" already\ncovers all subdomains, no dot needed). CsrfCookieFilter forces this\ncookie to resolve on every request, so this took down /actuator/health\nitself along with everything else, discovered only after deploying to\nthe real EC2/Tomcat stack - MockMvc''s test dispatcher doesn''t invoke\nTomcat''s cookie validation, so the existing test didn''t catch it.\n\nRequires updating the /toptrader/prod/csrf-cookie-domain SSM parameter\nvalue to match (done manually in AWS console, not part of this diff).","tree":{"sha":"79406c56c8ddc5218ea1706b0b097df8ebe88ac6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Efren707/toptrader/git/trees/79406c56c8ddc5218ea1706b0b097df8ebe88ac6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Efren707/toptrader/git/commits/d964e0e8b84e5aceff008d5f6bef21f4ebc9c8b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53492872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ef