/users/JungleM0nkey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JungleM0nkey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JungleM0nkey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JungleM0nkey/bonobo-terminal/commits/0623622a108f9fe7496cd0806d87360a6f157a6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T03:48:09Z","email":"ishevch@pm.me","name":"Ilya Shevchenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T03:48:09Z","email":"ishevch@pm.me","name":"Ilya Shevchenko"},"message":"feat(about): crypto donation card + official BMC widget\n\nAbout panel now offers two donation rails side-by-side:\n\n- New <CryptoAddressCard> with per-rail entries (Lightning + on-chain BTC),\n  color-coded leading icons (electric yellow for LN, Bitcoin orange for\n  on-chain), copy-to-clipboard with per-row check feedback, and full-\n  network hints to discourage paste-into-wrong-wallet errors. Long bech32\n  addresses use a truncated display while still copying the full string.\n\n- <SupportButton> rewritten to inject the official Buy Me a Coffee widget\n  (cdnjs script) instead of the hand-styled link. The widget emits its\n  markup via document.write/writeln, which silently no-ops post-load —\n  we intercept both APIs into a string buffer, parse via DOMParser (inert\n  doc, XSS-safe), and transplant the resulting nodes into our host. An\n  init guard makes the path StrictMode-safe so we never end up with two\n  scripts. Scaled to 0.55 via `zoom` so it reads as a peer affordance\n  next to the crypto card.\n\nAboutPanel layout: new .supportStack flex row holding the card on the\nleft and the BMC button on the right, vertically centered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0d6c1c5191eb68fc3c5a9eaf5c13ab5dae5c991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JungleM0nkey/bonobo-terminal/git/trees/d0d6c1c5191eb68fc3c5a9eaf5c13ab5dae5c991"},"url":"https://api.githu