"https://api.github.com/repos/JungleM0nkey/bonobo-terminal/commits/f5cea20e093a25acaec1d6ccb73e19d9f58cc1d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T03:12:04Z","email":"ishevch@pm.me","name":"Ilya Shevchenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T03:12:04Z","email":"ishevch@pm.me","name":"Ilya Shevchenko"},"message":"docs(claude): Capabilities subsystem section + post-Phase-G updates\n\nPhase F+G left CLAUDE.md stale in three places:\n- Services brief omitted services/hosts, services/capabilities, and\n  services/providers — the three folders the resolver model lives in.\n- \"External services\" section was titled with a path that no longer\n  exists (config/networkRegistry.ts deleted in Phase G#3).\n- No place documented the capability/binding/resolver model, the\n  Host.sshAlias contract, the always-on init path, or the hygiene\n  guard''s role.\n\nAdds a new \"Capabilities subsystem\" section between @bonobo/ui and\nExternal services. Covers:\n- Folder layout (hosts/, capabilities/, providers/) and what each owns.\n- Boot path (always runs post-Phase-G — no CAPABILITIES_BOOT_GATE) and\n  the migrateNetworkHosts → envBootstrap → seedHostLocal sequence.\n- The consumer rule: route through getCapabilitiesRuntime() instead of\n  hardcoded MELMBOX_HOST / \"melmbox\" / 192.168.30.50; the four files\n  in the melmboxLiteralsHygiene allowlist are the exceptions.\n- dropUnresolvedHostUrls() filter behavior when a host isn''t bound.\n- Operator action: bare host ids + sshAlias for ltx.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d533ab93d66cdf57c076ed5eb4b130c5ba54bf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JungleM0nkey/bonobo-terminal/git/trees/3d533ab93d66cdf57c076ed5eb4b130c5ba54bf0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JungleM0nkey/bonobo-terminal/git/commits/f5cea20e093a25acaec1d6ccb73e19d9f58cc1d9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"c