tions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/annminn104","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/annminn104/ncam.dev/commits/b6b368279d67f815073ac4e54ca304badcd40433/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:06:42Z","email":"annminn104@gmail.com","name":"annminn104"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:06:42Z","email":"annminn104@gmail.com","name":"annminn104"},"message":"feat(portfolio): move the home nav''s links into a drawer on mobile\n\nBelow 900px the five section links shared the bar with the brand and the\ntheme toggle as a horizontally scrolling row behind a fade, which showed\ntwo and a half of them. They now live in a drawer behind a menu button.\n\nThe drawer is a modal <dialog>, so focus containment, Escape and an\ninert page come from the browser. It is rendered beside the header, not\ninside it: .hnav''s backdrop-filter would make the header the containing\nblock of the fixed drawer while it animates out of the top layer.\n\nIt slides in from the right over a dimmed, blurred backdrop, its items\nfollowing one after another (--i), and slides back out: @starting-style\ncovers the way in, display and overlay transitioning with allow-discrete\nthe way out. Opening focuses the current section''s link, or the first;\na link (whose jump to its section then proceeds), the backdrop, Escape,\nthe close button and widening past the breakpoint all close it, and\nhtml:has(.hnav-drawer[open]) locks the page''s scroll meanwhile. Under\nreduced motion it opens and closes at once.","tree":{"sha":"e9f4fb8e8592b97fa1fbf1af7c46ccfc621c225a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/annminn104/ncam.dev/git/trees/e9f4fb8e8592b97fa1fbf1af7c46ccfc621c225a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/annminn104/ncam.dev/git/commits/b6b368279d67f815073ac4e54ca304badcd40433","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars