tarred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhillipT1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhillipT1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhillipT1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tpt-solutions/tpt-vertex/commits/f11d476b82493fc96f27b6e949d3dc7a0b078b56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:14:04Z","email":"43970944+PhillipT1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"PhillipT1"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:14:04Z","email":"43970944+PhillipT1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"PhillipT1"},"message":"Fix simulation crate regressions and update todo.md\n\nThe prior commit left tpt-vertex-simulation unable to compile its test\nsuite (missing import in adaptivity.rs), so several numerical bugs went\nuncaught: an inverted-winding test fixture in mass_props.rs, and a\ntransposed inverse-Jacobian in element.rs::shape_gradients that silently\nbroke the FEM patch test on any non-axis-aligned tetrahedron (masked by\na test that only exercised an axis-aligned reference element). Also\napplies cargo fmt/clippy cleanup across the crate.\n\nMarks the four remaining Phase 10 fast-follow items (nonlinear/large-\ndeformation, contact-coupled FEA, topology optimization, wasm execution)\nand the Phase 12 printer-connectivity items done in todo.md -- the crate\nand desktop/frontend integration already existed, the checklist was\njust stale.","tree":{"sha":"7ae887628fba72f9979d16ccb8e6dc63b178b085","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tpt-solutions/tpt-vertex/git/trees/7ae887628fba72f9979d16ccb8e6dc63b178b085"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tpt-solutions/tpt-vertex/git/commits/f11d476b82493fc96f27b6e949d3dc7a0b078b56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43970944?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phillip