"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"5cd515105ec660328d85448256793259d89ad77f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"authoredDate":"2026-03-21T13:10:18Z","committedDate":"2026-03-21T13:10:18Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"b8e04864cd1d2a8824fa4a28f12864496c8f3ac7"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"authoredDate":"2026-03-21T12:42:58Z","committedDate":"2026-03-21T12:42:58Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"59f7f0d7200e86fa0e62c34d0179f3daafe972d7"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"authoredDate":"2026-03-21T12:30:28Z","committedDate":"2026-03-21T12:30:28Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"f2747b53300777805d31e064a3a423c630fed73b"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"authoredDate":"2026-03-21T11:52:24Z","committedDate":"2026-03-21T11:52:24Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"dbf9ab14232052f8854d6cba29b25beecdf6b597"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"authoredDate":"2026-03-21T11:51:40Z","committedDate":"2026-03-21T11:51:40Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"0xnykcd@googlemail.com","name":"Nyk"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"9a4c7c7b3c69e960661129d010ca23e75dd01346"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"0xNyk","providerType":"User"},"email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"authoredDate":"2026-03-21T11:47:07Z","committedDate":"2026-03-21T11:47:07Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","repositoryId":1303564077,"sha":"311c7b06abec50c21f8b962f5226a9ccb1b26d76"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:47:30.596Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/commits/85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:59:40Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:59:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(recurring-tasks): include HH:MM in child title for sub-daily crons (#659)\n\nCloses #616.\n\nProblem\n-------\n\nRecurring tasks with sub-daily cron schedules (e.g. `0 * * * *` hourly,\n`*/5 * * * *` every-5-min) only spawned once per calendar day. All\nsubsequent spawns within the same day were silently skipped.\n\nRoot cause: `spawnRecurringTasks` derives child titles from\n`formatDateSuffix()` which only emitted day-level granularity (`MMM DD`).\nThe duplicate-prevention guard at recurring-tasks.ts:75-79 then matches\non `(title, workspace_id, project_id)` and finds the previous spawn,\nreturning early.\n\nFix\n---\n\n  1. New `isSubDailyCron(cronExpr)` helper returns true when the\n     minute or hour field is anything other than a single concrete\n     number (covers wildcards, ranges, lists, steps).\n\n  2. `formatDateSuffix(now, subDaily)` now takes an explicit `now`\n     and a `subDaily` flag:\n\n        Daily / weekly / monthly:  \"Apr 24\"           (unchanged)\n        Sub-daily:                 \"Apr 24, 13:35\"\n\n     Same-day spawns at 13:00 and 14:00 now produce different titles\n     and the duplicate-guard correctly admits both.\n\n  3. Daily/weekly/monthly title format is preserved so existing\n     operator workflows don''t see a title-churn migration.\n\nCompatibility\n-------------\n\n  - `isCronDue()` already prevents same-minute double-spawns via the\n    `lastSpawnedAtMs` check, so this PR doesn''t loosen the dedup —\n    it just stops the dedup from firing on the *wrong* layer.\n\n  - The `formatDateSuffix` signature now takes optional arguments\n    with sane defaults; existing call sites still work.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n13 new tests in src/lib/__tests__/recurring-tasks.test.ts:\n\n  - `isSubDailyCron` recognizes hourly / every-5-min / every-minute /\n    ranged-minute crons; rejects daily/weekly; defensive on malformed.\n  - `formatDateSuffix` returns `MMM DD` (daily) and `MMM DD, HH:MM`\n    (sub-daily); zero-pads day-of-month.\n  - Regression: two hourly spawns on the same day produce different titles.\n  - Regression: every-5-min spawns within the same hour produce different titles.\n  - Daily cron preserves historical \"MMM DD\" shape.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"635aefae71845767a0277a3160a1260b9bd76776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/git/trees/635aefae71845767a0277a3160a1260b9bd76776"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/git/commits/85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 635aefae71845767a0277a3160a1260b9bd76776\nparent 0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1778129980 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778129980 +0700\n\nfix(recurring-tasks): include HH:MM in child title for sub-daily crons (#659)\n\nCloses #616.\n\nProblem\n-------\n\nRecurring tasks with sub-daily cron schedules (e.g. `0 * * * *` hourly,\n`*/5 * * * *` every-5-min) only spawned once per calendar day. All\nsubsequent spawns within the same day were silently skipped.\n\nRoot cause: `spawnRecurringTasks` derives child titles from\n`formatDateSuffix()` which only emitted day-level granularity (`MMM DD`).\nThe duplicate-prevention guard at recurring-tasks.ts:75-79 then matches\non `(title, workspace_id, project_id)` and finds the previous spawn,\nreturning early.\n\nFix\n---\n\n  1. New `isSubDailyCron(cronExpr)` helper returns true when the\n     minute or hour field is anything other than a single concrete\n     number (covers wildcards, ranges, lists, steps).\n\n  2. `formatDateSuffix(now, subDaily)` now takes an explicit `now`\n     and a `subDaily` flag:\n\n        Daily / weekly / monthly:  \"Apr 24\"           (unchanged)\n        Sub-daily:                 \"Apr 24, 13:35\"\n\n     Same-day spawns at 13:00 and 14:00 now produce different titles\n     and the duplicate-guard correctly admits both.\n\n  3. Daily/weekly/monthly title format is preserved so existing\n     operator workflows don''t see a title-churn migration.\n\nCompatibility\n-------------\n\n  - `isCronDue()` already prevents same-minute double-spawns via the\n    `lastSpawnedAtMs` check, so this PR doesn''t loosen the dedup —\n    it just stops the dedup from firing on the *wrong* layer.\n\n  - The `formatDateSuffix` signature now takes optional arguments\n    with sane defaults; existing call sites still work.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n13 new tests in src/lib/__tests__/recurring-tasks.test.ts:\n\n  - `isSubDailyCron` recognizes hourly / every-5-min / every-minute /\n    ranged-minute crons; rejects daily/weekly; defensive on malformed.\n  - `formatDateSuffix` returns `MMM DD` (daily) and `MMM DD, HH:MM`\n    (sub-daily); zero-pads day-of-month.\n  - Regression: two hourly spawns on the same day produce different titles.\n  - Regression: every-5-min spawns within the same hour produce different titles.\n  - Daily cron preserves historical \"MMM DD\" shape.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/Bw8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmAAQAHRkazx8b1OkBlF1VNo3/jDS\nOgJHGuXEeMi3KTrH2wMJ3sYjA3jyoxQYC5IhLBqMT1d8earjowsBbilFRmXnP66n\nID4nCwfUS9S+LSgvQRMMBNrZp8tvjz0Mnr1GG5DBtOIAc6UqEe/sj/8yC0nO2IBC\nTHuMH1hSQ0R5EeLAudYs1PkFpNfr2C+kCKhDyYO6+v1QPZI1Z2w/fDTN8VZurRS3\n7d8fhmsiQRIpbl1LebmBDYE2oF27Tupc7Jn4klTbmjPAjqJDgrAAuCUMi8QYayAf\nwEJtSh3l/zZTnGbqOxlZHjbneY/ttOm4g2sxW/AsP5R3kbjjbIxJI6XjrsQpV9+k\nEoKhBLUxUQRyVz17/6jXhQbz9PpOkVC/EwGaDrWTnDR+HCW8WWHdj9NlP8b4u47z\n8VijqtP67dLLVLzzscwyLaFKAieneHZmU8PuYbHrkqXXaP05MimeYlMjDrxvU5rG\nU2E3jj7ZfDy0jQQWZ2a3dZA6k5v1gnOqiK+XY7QxptsSYht8l/2hM9YOe021m0qT\ngbmfpgQwrMPEgr9vjoLusA+fGOqnuhLemjRtVVPOSCEXmOe2NtCwe42OwINqD0aN\nsG6FR9IVSxtF6nWU7s12rSviwoRgVW9NddJ9FOfI0YmbHCLcIrx3bSvSyxr6QI7g\n4tVSDO7PHPbXkfzAo+um\n=k6BL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T04:40:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/commit/85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a","node_id":"C_kwDOTbLPLdoAKDg1MjE1YzU3N2Y0OTFjZjU3MGFhNjY3ZTY3NTdkOGIzMGUyMDFkMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/commit/0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0","sha":"0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/commits/0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0"}],"sha":"85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/commits/85215c577f491cf570aa667e6757d8b30e201d0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/commits/0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:59:34Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:59:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(openclaw-doctor): single-flight + 30s TTL cache to prevent CPU/RAM spikes (#658)\n\nCloses #613.\n\nProblem\n-------\n\n`GET /api/openclaw/doctor` spawns a Node subprocess that allocates\n~300-600 MB and runs at 37-51 % CPU. The dashboard banner + the\nonboarding modal + multiple browser tabs polling concurrently could\nproduce 6+ simultaneous subprocesses on a 4 GB host (issue #613\nobserved combined CPU ~89 %, RAM ~3.5 GB).\n\nFix\n---\n\nTwo layers of mitigation, GET-only:\n\n  1. Single-flight: if a doctor invocation is already in flight,\n     concurrent callers share its eventual result — never spawn a\n     second subprocess while one is running.\n\n  2. TTL cache: cache the last response for MC_DOCTOR_TTL_MS\n     (30 s default; settable via env, 0 disables caching for tests).\n     Subsequent GETs within the window return the cached payload.\n\nCache invalidation\n------------------\n\n  - `POST /api/openclaw/doctor` (the --fix path) calls\n    `invalidateDoctorCache()` after a successful fix so the freshly-\n    fixed state surfaces immediately rather than waiting out the TTL.\n  - \"Not installed\" errors are NOT cached — the operator may install\n    OpenClaw mid-session and we want the next poll to pick that up.\n  - The POST/--fix subprocess is intentionally uncoalesced because\n    operators clicking \"Re-check\" want a guaranteed fresh run.\n\nResponse headers\n----------------\n\n  - `X-Doctor-Cache: hit` | `miss` so dashboards can confirm the\n    coalescing is working.\n  - `X-Doctor-Age-Ms: <n>` on cache hits.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n6 new tests in src/lib/__tests__/openclaw-doctor-route.test.ts:\n\n  - Concurrent GETs collapse to a single runOpenClaw invocation\n  - Cache hits within TTL skip the subprocess\n  - TTL=0 forces re-run on every GET\n  - \"Not installed\" errors are not cached\n  - Unauthenticated requests reject before subprocess spawn\n  - invalidateDoctorCache() drops the cache on demand\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"299f921a9c72ee5d9fa18dc5a82ec68a463d2256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/git/trees/299f921a9c72ee5d9fa18dc5a82ec68a463d2256"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devSubho51347/mission-control-dashboard/git/commits/0f0ec68976c3662d3279821c1ed701209e4d85f0","verification":{"payload":"tree 299f921a9c72ee5d9fa18dc5a82ec68a463d2256\nparent a34d4c868f5eb13789472fdeb8bb53be1dc55082\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1778129974 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778129974 +0700\n\nfix(openclaw-doctor): single-flight + 30s TTL cache to prevent CPU/RAM spikes (#658)\n\nCloses #613.\n\nProblem\n-------\n\n`GET /api/openclaw/doctor` spawns a Node subprocess that allocates\n~300-600 MB and runs at 37-51 % CPU. The dashboard banner + the\nonboarding modal + multiple browser tabs polling concurrently could\nproduce 6+ simultaneous subprocesses on a 4 GB host (issue #613\nobserved combined CPU ~89 %, RAM ~3.5 GB).\n\nFix\n---\n\nTwo layers of mitigation, GET-only:\n\n  1. Single-flight: if a doctor invocation is already in flight,\n     concurrent callers share its eventual result — never spawn a\n     second subprocess while one is running.\n\n  2. TTL cache: cache the last response for MC_DOCTOR_TTL_MS\n     (30 s default; settable via env, 0 disables caching for tests).\n     Subsequent GETs within the window return the cached payload.\n\nCache invalidation\n------------------\n\n  - `POST /api/openclaw/doctor` (the --fix path) calls\n    `invalidateDoctorCache()` after a successful fix so the freshly-\n    fixed state surfaces immediately rather than waiting out the TTL.\n  - \"Not installed\" errors are NOT cached — the operator may install\n    OpenClaw mid-session and we want the next poll to pick that up.\n  - The POST/--fix subprocess is intentionally uncoalesced because\n    operators clicking \"Re-check\" want a guaranteed fresh run.\n\nResponse headers\n----------------\n\n  - `X-Doctor-Cache: hit` | `miss` so dashboards can confirm the\n    coalescing is working.\n  - `X-Doctor-Age-Ms: <n>` on cache hits.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n6 new tests in src/lib/__tests__/openclaw-doctor-route.test.ts:\n\n  - Concurrent GETs collapse to a single runOpenClaw invocation\n  - Cache hits within TTL skip the subprocess\n  - TTL=0 forces re-run on every GET\n  - \"Not installed\" errors are not cached\n  - Unauthenticated requests reject before subprocess spawn\n  - invalidateDoctorCache() drops the cache on demand\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/Bw2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7NMQADB6+ZHZnV5+Z45tW0Aw0aoB\n0y0s8I5ZmR4KQsqCdGRFSyAQ9VbN5N9YvjJi54drsSfKoYyMM4ijyrH/egSBux/A\ncRVVlEj4vhUStDgDsRV84whf+2/YjA34h+J9lXJdSAgP/k6jncw3PDNqyQ2b2lFm\n4xMIiI7h19WOdchFwN+PSzRqPAm5UbuEflCW38lECy5j0CBwcc1pZGnKnGOkQAv0\nJO3Zm6UPF3wFXBgv64v/hxAzgXcgoVf/MQvEUDlQ8dlvjfkokgiZeQRnYqr/0rkw\nvFsjGVKq/OgPMvkSGi/MsefwkH8KOunanCR4P16xRQbCNLe4vibXFopNOySwF3C5\nN9DthoVH4b8aW1+GivBuxnPP19Xori5OtE9yhFSZ5zNgqPF7sCSmtzuj+2rmparF\nrzafv8HQ6MGRArZ4rgFgMUZCR4EEf2GTRQDqCFannyZ/2CwDX/pAT4tgNuSbjEgZ\nWAt5CtX