,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/95b70a035d454ec423881de9732a0d2b4fdae65b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T09:11:16Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T09:11:16Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Redesign Main Dashboard as a Control Center (from upstream frontend c006ce0cd)\n\nPorts the \"Control Center\" MainDashboard/ActivityFeed redesign from\npilot-voice-agent-frontend@c006ce0cd''s monolithic TranscriptOverlay.tsx into\nPILOT''s split-file transcript/MainDashboard.tsx. Scoped to the dashboard UI\nonly — the Customer Care/CSR-observer portion of that same upstream commit\nis intentionally excluded (already declined earlier: overlaps with PILOT''s\nTwilio-based Customer Resolution feature).\n\nBackend: added GET /api/v1/sessions/stats (real SQL aggregation over\nSession/TranscriptLog/AuditLog for the new metric tiles), adapted to PILOT''s\nactual audit convention (AuditLog.action == \"policy_check\", not upstream''s\n\"tool_call\"). avg_latency_ms returns null when there''s nothing to average\n(PILOT''s policy_check rows don''t populate latency_ms) rather than fabricating\na number; the tile shows \"—\" in that case.\n\nFrontend: new layout — status chips + pipeline detail modal, a 3-column\nLive Transcript / Current Task+Queue / Agent-working step trace, 4 metric\ntiles backed by /stats, and a Sessions + Activity Feed row. Local building\nblocks (StatusChip, SectionCard, StepRow, MetricTile, PipelineDetailModal)\nlive directly in MainDashboard.tsx rather than shared helpers, since no\nother view uses them yet. Adapted for PILOT''s real useSession() shape (no\nwakeActive/isStreaming fields upstream has) and corrected the pipeline\nstage descriptions to PILOT''s actual models (qwen2.5:7b, large-v3-turbo)\ninstead of copying upstream''s config verbatim.\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit, npx vite build, backend py_compile + import.","tree":{"sha":"7ac80eb036778e90f38a4144fc76b949ee6ceaf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/7ac80eb036778e90f38a4144fc76b949ee6ceaf0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/95b70a035d454ec423881de9732a0d2b4fdae65b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/95b70a035d454ec423881de9732a0d2b4fdae65b","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKDk1YjcwYTAzNWQ0NTRlYzQyMzg4MWRlOTczMmEwZDJiNGZkYWU2NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1","sha":"30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1"}],"sha":"95b70a035d454ec423881de9732a0d2b4fdae65b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/95b70a035d454ec423881de9732a0d2b4fdae65b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T08:57:58Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T08:57:58Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Update PPT Copilot from upstream: WYSIWYG canvas editor + slide reorder\n\nBoth upstream branches had moved forward since the original transfer\n(backend 869dd08d9 -> c3a22cfc3, frontend feature/ppt-view@bba05b6a2 ->\nfeature/PPT-Copilot@d22ea5949). Pulled the PPT-specific pieces from both;\nexplicitly left out the rest (see below).\n\nFrontend — this was the bigger gap: the backend''s WYSIWYG shape-editing\nendpoints (shape-style, shape-add-text, shape, shape-zorder) were already\nin PILOT from the original transfer, but the matching frontend UI never\nwas, because the original transfer used feature/ppt-view (Jul 10), a\nbranch that predates it — feature/PPT-Copilot (Jul 11) has the actual\ncanvas UI commit. Added:\n- components/PPTView.tsx: full WYSIWYG canvas (drag/resize/rotate shapes,\n  floating format toolbar — bold/italic/underline/font/size/color/align,\n  add text box, delete shape, bring-to-front/send-to-back, image\n  replacement), now the default editing view.\n- components/Icons.tsx (new): the stroke-based icon set the new toolbar\n  uses.\n- store/types.ts: SlideShape/SlideInfo extended with the fields the canvas\n  needs (shape_id, italic, underline, font, height, rotation, type,\n  slide_width/height).\n\nBackend:\n- tools/ppt_copilot.py: new ppt_reorder_slide tool (\"move slide 2 after\n  slide 5\"/\"move the third slide to the front\"); ppt_add_slide now\n  auto-picks a sensible insertion point via LLM when the user doesn''t say\n  one (previously always appended at the end), understands \"on/at/as slide\n  N\" and ordinal phrasing (\"as the third slide\") for explicit placement,\n  and coerces an invalid/blank generated slide kind to the GD template''s\n  \"text\" kind instead of risking an off-brand slide.\n- api/ppt.py: reorder_slide_fast_async (XML-only reorder + kinds/sources\n  sidecar bookkeeping, paired with the existing background thumbnail\n  refresh).\n- services/ppt_template_builder.py: reorder_slide_in_deck, pick_insert_\n  position (the LLM call behind ppt_add_slide''s auto-positioning); deck/\n  slide generation now goes through the new priority gate below instead of\n  a bare asyncio.to_thread.\n- core/llm_gate.py (new): a prioritized Ollama dispatcher — background PPT\n  generation (many serial LLM calls) now yields the Ollama slot to\n  latency-critical Front-LLM voice routing instead of starving it, the\n  root cause upstream describes as \"Ollama classify error: timed out on\n  every turn while a PPT generates.\"\n- registry.py, tools/policy.py, pipeline/front_llm.py, services/front_llm.py:\n  wire ppt_reorder_slide through the same path every other PPT tool\n  already uses (registration, RBAC per role, arg schema, routing prompt).\n- Fixed a real bug in the upstream source: ppt_reorder_slide''s success path\n  called get_state(session_id) without importing it — every other\n  function in the file imports it locally first. Would have raised\n  NameError on the first successful reorder; added the missing import.\n\nDeliberately NOT pulled — out of scope for \"PPT Copilot\" and directly\noverlaps with the Twilio-integrated Customer Resolution feature built\nearlier today: the same upstream commit (c3a22cfc3 / c006ce0cd) also\ncontains a large customer-care redesign (services/care_observer.py,\nservices/react_agent.py, a \"PILOT is now a silent observer, no TTS on\nlive calls\" behavior change, a modified tools/resolution_tool.py, a new\napi/care.py, and a Control-Center/Customer-Care dashboard redesign in\nfrontend TranscriptOverlay.tsx — which doesn''t map onto PILOT''s already-\nsplit component structure). Flagging this separately rather than merging\nit silently, since it would change customercare call behavior underneath\nthe calling/sentiment work already wired up.\n\nVerified: backend/main.py imports cleanly, ppt_reorder_slide is\nregistered, _parse_insert_position/_parse_reorder tested directly against\nseveral real phrasings with correct results; frontend tsc --noEmit and\nvite build both pass clean.","tree":{"sha":"5595b5805cb0e0719aa038fbb7bc262d939159f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/5595b5805cb0e0719aa038fbb7bc262d939159f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKDMwYzIwOTY4NTMzYzY2OTYyYzA2ODIwY2M5ODE2NGRkMzRmODQ0YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd","sha":"71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd"}],"sha":"30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/30c20968533c66962c06820cc98164dd34f844c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T07:20:26Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T07:20:26Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Add real two-party calling to Customer Resolution (Twilio Voice)\n\nCustomer Resolution previously only worked on a single browser microphone\n(diarization guessing \"customer\" vs \"rep\" from one audio stream, nested\nunder the \"Trip Planner\" page since that''s the only customercare-usecase\nsession PILOT had). This adds actual telephony: the rep talks through the\nbrowser (Twilio Voice JS SDK / WebRTC), Twilio bridges that to a real PSTN\ncall to the customer''s phone number, and the live call audio streams back\ninto the same ASR/sentiment/resolution pipeline in real time.\n\nBackend:\n- services/twilio_client.py: Voice access token generation (for the rep''s\n  browser client) and Twilio webhook signature validation.\n- api/telephony.py: GET /token (rep''s access token) and POST /voice (TwiML\n  webhook — Twilio calls this the moment the browser client places a call;\n  validates the Twilio signature, registers a real customercare session,\n  and returns TwiML that both starts a Media Stream and dials the\n  customer''s real number, bridging the two legs).\n- api/ws_telephony.py: new /ws/telephony/{session_id} WebSocket receiving\n  Twilio''s live call audio (8kHz mu-law, base64, ~20ms frames, tagged by\n  track). Twilio''s inbound/outbound track tag gives an exact customer-vs-\n  rep split — a hard signal from the telephony layer, not a diarization\n  guess. Decodes + upsamples to 16kHz PCM (matching what services/stt.py\n  expects), transcribes in ~2.5s windows per track, and feeds transcripts\n  through the same add_span/sentiment-scoring path pipeline/asr_worker.py\n  already uses for browser-mic turns — Customer Resolution''s live panels\n  work unchanged regardless of which audio source populated them.\n- tools/resolution_tool.py: _customer_transcript() now also excludes\n  \"REP\"/\"AGENT\" roles (previously only excluded \"PILOT\") — a real human\n  rep''s own speech on a call must not count as \"customer\" transcript.\n- main.py: registers both new routers; exempts /telephony/voice from the\n  Bearer-token auth middleware (Twilio can''t send one — the handler\n  validates the Twilio signature itself instead).\n- core/config.py: TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID/AUTH_TOKEN/API_KEY_SID/API_KEY_SECRET/\n  TWIML_APP_SID/PHONE_NUMBER, and PUBLIC_BASE_URL (Twilio must reach this\n  backend over the real internet — never localhost; needs a tunnel like\n  ngrok for local dev, a real domain for anything beyond that).\n\nFrontend:\n- ResolutionView.tsx: new \"Call Customer\" panel (phone number input, Call/\n  Hang Up), using @twilio/voice-sdk to register the rep''s browser as a\n  Twilio Voice client and place the call.\n\nRequires external setup only the user can do: a Twilio account, a\npurchased phone number, and (for local dev) a public tunnel — none of\nwhich exist yet, so live calling isn''t testable until that''s in place.\nVerified what''s testable now: backend imports cleanly, /telephony/token\nreturns a clean 503 with setup instructions when unconfigured (rather than\na raw crash), and both `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` pass clean on the\nfrontend with the new Twilio Voice SDK dependency.","tree":{"sha":"d9501649af96d85a29907076857e8565d267e40d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/d9501649af96d85a29907076857e8565d267e40d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKDcxZGNiNTRiMGI4MGNlMzhlM2VmZjNhMTJmMTYzNjI0ZTNlZDhiYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83","sha":"ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83"}],"sha":"71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/71dcb54b0b80ce38e3eff3a12f163624e3ed8bbd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T06:45:11Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T06:45:11Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"fix: Google SSO could reach the dashboard without completing voice enrollment\n\nGoogle SSO auto-registers a user with is_active=True and issues a fully\nvalid token immediately, with no voice sample of its own. Normal signup\ncan''t do this — it captures the voice sample *before* OTP verification,\nbefore any token exists, so a token literally can''t exist without\nenrollment. Google''s flow had no equivalent gate at all: it went straight\nto the dashboard, and the /enroll page''s Cancel button just did\nstore.setPage(\"dashboard\") client-side with no server check.\n\nThree separate bugs, fixed together:\n\n1. Enrollment done via the /enroll page (VoiceCalibration) never linked to\n   the logged-in user. /enrollment/audio only auto-links a VoiceEnrollment\n   row via the email + PENDING_SIGNUPS path (pre-account signup); the\n   VoiceCalibration flow sends neither, so the row''s user_id stayed null\n   forever — even a Google user who fully completed enrollment was never\n   actually voice-identifiable. Now accepts an optional Bearer token and\n   links to that user when present.\n\n2. No has_enrollment signal existed anywhere. Added it to every auth\n   response (login, google-login, verify-otp, verify-forgot-otp), computed\n   from a real VoiceEnrollment(user_id=..., status=\"ready\") row.\n\n3. No enforcement. Added a render-level gate in app.tsx — re-evaluated on\n   every page change, not just at login — that forces unenrolled accounts\n   to /enroll regardless of how `page` got set to something else (stale\n   URL, back/forward, the Cancel button, anything). The Google login\n   callback now also routes to /enroll instead of /dashboard on first\n   login. The Cancel button signs out instead of \"cancelling\" into a\n   dashboard the gate would just bounce it back out of; and enrollment\n   completion now updates the client-side user object immediately (the\n   gate reads it live and had no way to know the DB just changed).\n\nAlso fixed a pre-existing, unrelated bug this surfaced: /enrollment/start\nand /enrollment/audio weren''t in the auth middleware''s public-path\nexemption list, which would have blocked the *anonymous* pre-signup\nenrollment step (normal signup, before OTP, before any token) entirely.\n\nVerified live end-to-end: fresh Google login -> has_enrollment: false ->\ncompleted enrollment via /enrollment/audio with a Bearer token -> DB row\ncorrectly linked (user_id=8, status=ready) -> next login returns\nhas_enrollment: true.","tree":{"sha":"1d73281e3923f26aa27eccf9962199337b449643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/1d73281e3923f26aa27eccf9962199337b449643"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKGZmM2JiMzhjOTQ5NWMzNGVjMTA3ZDA0ODMxNmRkYmI3ODhlODRhODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a","sha":"0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a"}],"sha":"ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/ff3bb38c9495c34ec107d048316ddbb788e84a83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T06:20:01Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T06:20:01Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"fix: escalate button appeared broken after assessing an empty conversation\n\nresolution_assess() honestly returns just {\"spoken_reply\": \"...\"} (no\nrecommendation/confidence/etc.) when there''s no customer conversation yet\nto assess. runAssess() was calling setResolution(res) on that unconditionally,\nso the assessment panel rendered anyway with every field undefined —\nconfidence showed NaN%, the recommendation badge silently defaulted to\n\"Resolvable\" (undefined !== \"escalate\"), and the Escalate button appeared\non top of that bogus card, which is what made it look non-functional.\n\nNow only treats the response as a real assessment when it actually has a\nrecommendation field; otherwise shows the honest spoken_reply as an info\nmessage and leaves the assessment panel in its empty state, so Escalate\nonly ever appears attached to a real assessment.\n\nVerified /api/v1/resolution/escalate itself works correctly end-to-end\n(created a real ticket) — the bug was purely in when the button rendered,\nnot the escalation logic.","tree":{"sha":"7b826cd8155bb2d00cf7bda54440acb7f840089f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/7b826cd8155bb2d00cf7bda54440acb7f840089f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKDBkYmQwY2I4MTMwYmIxODEyMDUyMTFjYmZlNTViN2Q3NGRhNWQzOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e","sha":"c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e"}],"sha":"0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/0dbd0cb8130bb181205211cbfe55b7d74da5d38a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T06:16:08Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T06:16:08Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"fix: Assess/Escalate buttons on Customer Resolution silently disabled with no session\n\nBoth buttons were disabled whenever sessionId was null (no active voice\nsession) with no visual indication why — same amber \"enabled\" styling\nwhether actually clickable or not, so a click just did nothing. sessionId\nstays null until the user starts the mic bar at the bottom of the page;\nthe lightweight background WS connection that would otherwise populate it\n(shared_voice.ts''s ensureConnected()) is only ever called from the\ndisabled Wanna Chat page, so it never fires here.\n\nAdded an inline banner explaining what to do, and fixed the disabled\nbutton styling (opacity/cursor) to actually look disabled instead of\nlooking identical to the enabled state.\n\nVerified the underlying flow works once a session exists: created a real\nsession via /api/v1/sessions and confirmed /api/v1/resolution/assess\nreturns 200 against it.","tree":{"sha":"126269f24c42e34ca84508618d3cdb37fd0c8501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/126269f24c42e34ca84508618d3cdb37fd0c8501"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKGMyMjI5NTc3MTQzNzJiODVmZWU2NWJmY2ZiYTMyYzc5ZmRjOTA5OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79","sha":"4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79"}],"sha":"c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/c222957714372b85fee65bfcfba32c79fdc9099e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T05:59:11Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T05:59:11Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Customer Resolution: upgrade sentiment/KB search to real models, fix Groq bug\n\nInstalls and pins the previously-missing dependencies for Customer\nResolution''s optional (but higher-quality) code paths, which were silently\nrunning in their degraded fallback modes:\n\n- torch + sentence-transformers + faiss-cpu: services/sentiment.py and\n  services/kb_index.py were built to use real models but degrade to a\n  keyword heuristic / substring match when torch/sentence-transformers/\n  faiss aren''t installed — which was the actual state. Verified live:\n  sentiment now runs the real cardiffnlp/twitter-roberta model, KB search\n  now runs real semantic embeddings (both confirmed via direct test runs\n  producing correctly-classified/ranked real output).\n- groq 0.9.0 -> 1.5.0: the old version''s AsyncClient construction was\n  incompatible with the already-installed httpx 0.28.1\n  (\"unexpected keyword argument ''proxies''\"), breaking the Groq rung of the\n  Ollama -> Gemini -> Groq reasoning fallback chain used by\n  services/session_summary.py. Verified the client now constructs cleanly.\n\nNone of this was strictly required — Ollama is live and was already\ncarrying the LLM reasoning load, and both services degrade gracefully\nwithout their optional dependencies — but all three are now running in\ntheir intended real mode instead of fallback mode.","tree":{"sha":"5dcff0debc72a96cc3ddad1d529ba5504a91008c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/5dcff0debc72a96cc3ddad1d529ba5504a91008c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKDRiNDk2OTA2Y2E0NWRiZGE3ZDkzZDZhNDgzZjkxMTQxNDczZjlhNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418","sha":"f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418"}],"sha":"4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/4b496906ca45dbda7d93d6a483f91141473f9a79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T05:49:06Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T05:49:06Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Trip Planner: real-time hotel/flight/train search, no fabricated data\n\nReplaces the fabricated fallback data throughout the Trip Planner''s hotel\nand train search (hardcoded named hotel lists per city, a Kota->Kolkata\n\"connecting route\" with invented intermediate stations, a Chennai default\nfor \"near my location\", formula-based fake prices/ratings) with real,\nlive-sourced search — honestly reporting no results rather than inventing\nthem when nothing real is found.\n\nHotels (tools/flight_booking.py, services/amadeus_client.py — new):\n- _search_hotels_real(): real geolocation (lat/lng) -> Amadeus Hotel Search\n  (real prices, official star rating) tried first, Google Places Nearby\n  Search (real name/rating/address, no price) as fallback, live Tavily web\n  search as the last resort when neither structured API is reachable.\n  Never fabricates a price or rating — returns however many genuine\n  results exist, including zero.\n- Deleted _generate_proximity_hotels() and both hardcoded per-city hotel\n  lists (the Chennai list, the generic brand-name substitution + formula\n  pricing) that lived in the old Tavily-empty and MCP-response branches.\n- \"Near my location\" now requires real coordinates (browser Geolocation\n  API) or honestly asks for a city — no more defaulting to Chennai.\n- Star-rating filtering (\"5 star hotels\") parsed from the query or passed\n  explicitly, applied against Amadeus''s official rating / Places'' user\n  rating.\n\nTrains (tools/flight_booking.py):\n- _search_trains_real(): real direct-train search via live web search\n  first; when none parse as genuine, live-derives a connecting interchange\n  city (asks a live search, verifies the answer is a real place via\n  geocoding — never picked from a fixed \"major junction\" list) and\n  searches both legs independently.\n- Deleted _generate_train_segments() and its three hardcoded itineraries\n  (Kota->Chennai via Itarsi with invented intermediate stops/times, a\n  Chennai<->Kolkata express, and a generic template with fake \"Suburb Stn\"\n  placeholder station names), plus the duplicate hardcoded Kota->Kolkata\n  and Kota->Prayagraj train lists in the MCP-response branch.\n\nFlights (tools/flight_booking.py):\n- _search_duffel() now sorts the full offer set by real price before\n  truncating to 5, so \"cheapest flight\" actually reflects Duffel''s lowest\n  fare rather than API-default order. Fixed a latent null-safety bug this\n  testing surfaced (`response.json().get(\"data\", {})` doesn''t protect\n  against an explicit `\"data\": null`).\n\nFrontend (CustomerCareView.tsx):\n- Added real browser Geolocation capture (\"📡 Near me\" button) for hotel\n  search, with typed-city fallback on denial/unavailability (no default\n  city). Added a min-rating selector wired to the new backend filter.\n- Deleted the frontend''s own hardcoded train segment fallback (the same\n  Kota->Chennai and Chennai<->Kolkata itineraries, duplicated client-side)\n  — replaced with an honest single-leg render of the train''s real\n  name/code/times when the backend doesn''t provide a multi-leg breakdown.\n- Hotel price now shows \"Check rates\" instead of blank when a source\n  (Places, live search) has no real nightly rate rather than a number.\n\nKnown limitations found during this work (not fixable in code):\n- AMADEUS_CLIENT_ID/SECRET in .env are still the literal placeholder\n  values from .env.example — Amadeus''s real hotel-price path is wired up\n  and tested working code-wise, but returns nothing until real credentials\n  are added.\n- GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY in .env doesn''t match Google''s key format (AIzaSy...)\n  and is rejected by both Places and Geocoding — likely the wrong\n  credential was pasted into that variable. Hotels currently fall back to\n  live web search (real names, honest about missing price/rating) until\n  this is fixed.\n- Train search is intentionally strict (requires a real 5-digit train\n  number + name in the source text) and will report \"no results\" more\n  often than the old fake system did — that''s by design, not a bug.\n\nVerified: backend/main.py imports cleanly; frontend tsc --noEmit and vite\nbuild both pass clean; hotel and flight search tested live end-to-end\nagainst real Duffel/Tavily/Nominatim APIs.","tree":{"sha":"2af6764616e3b1b3e529f8ab438c6fd4e7ef011f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/2af6764616e3b1b3e529f8ab438c6fd4e7ef011f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKGYxYjY1MjVmNTY0ZTM4ZjQ4YjJlYjA1NjNlZWQzOTJmZWRiY2U0MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45","sha":"be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45"}],"sha":"f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/f1b6525f564e38f48b2eb0563eed392fedbce418"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T18:02:14Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T18:02:14Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Re-enable Meeting TALKINIA feature in UI navigation\n\nUncomments the Meeting TALKINIA wiring that was previously disabled from UI\nnavigation: Sidebar nav entry, Main Dashboard tools quick-link, the\nDashboard route/view in transcript/index.tsx, URL routing (/meetings deep\nlinks, protectedPaths, dashPages) and the Talkinia iframe postMessage\nlistener in app.tsx.\n\nNothing here was actually deleted before — MeetingsPageView.tsx, the store\nslices (talkiniaSubRoute etc.), and the backend voice-routing fast path\n(\"go to meetings\" / \"talkinia\" -> navigate_page) were already fully intact;\nonly the UI entry points were commented out. Email Center and Wanna Chat\nremain disabled, as only Meeting TALKINIA was requested.\n\nMeeting TALKINIA is a separate Next.js app (TALKINIA_STREAM/) expected on\nlocalhost:3000 — not started by `make dev`/`make frontend-dev`, run it\nseparately if you want the iframe to actually load content.","tree":{"sha":"595736117985db4774cc831db7e7a8412eacca91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/595736117985db4774cc831db7e7a8412eacca91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKGJlMDIyMmUxNGMyMjAwMjQ3Y2JiNmIwNjI4MjViNDg0ZTRmNmNiNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4","sha":"b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4"}],"sha":"be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/be0222e14c2200247cbb6b062825b484e4f6cb45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T17:56:07Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T17:56:07Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"fix: migrate pre-existing tickets table to add Customer Resolution columns\n\nThe dev DB already had a `tickets` table (predating the Ticket model, missing\npriority/escalated/escalation_target) from earlier, unrelated work.\ncreate_all() only creates tables that don''t exist yet, so it silently left\nthe stale schema in place — ticket_create (and escalate_ticket, which calls\nit) failed with \"no such column: tickets.priority\" on every call, breaking\nCustomer Resolution end-to-end. Added a migrate_tickets_cols() step,\nfollowing the same ALTER-TABLE-if-missing pattern already used for\nusers.status.\n\nVerified live against the running dev server: /api/v1/resolution/assess and\n/api/v1/resolution/escalate both return 200 now.","tree":{"sha":"4917059699347440a1844acdc64b6fdf941b4645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/4917059699347440a1844acdc64b6fdf941b4645"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKGIxN2I5NTY1YTIzM2Y1YmRmNjMzMjI0OTA1YTI3YTg3OTI4Y2Q2YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9","sha":"f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9"}],"sha":"b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/b17b9565a233f5bdf633224905a27a87928cd6a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T17:45:30Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T17:45:30Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Add Customer Resolution as a new feature, transferred from the upstream backend\n\nAdds a standalone \"Customer Resolution\" feature — live CSR-dashboard\nresolution/escalation assessment — sourced from both previously given\ndirectories (pilot-voice-agent-backend-869dd..., which had the full engine;\npilot-voice-agent-frontend-bba05... had no UI for it, so the dashboard page\nis new). Does not touch the existing Trip Planner feature (flight_booking.py,\napi/flights.py, travel_planner.py, api/travel.py, CustomerCareView.tsx —\nall unmodified).\n\nBackend (new files, import paths rewritten to PILOT''s `backend.` prefix):\n- services/sentiment.py — per-turn customer frustration/urgency scoring\n- services/kb_index.py — semantic KB search (FAISS + sentence-transformers,\n  falls back to substring match if the embedder can''t load)\n- services/session_summary.py — shared Ollama/Gemini/Groq LLM chain, issue\n  synopsis generation\n- services/resolution.py — resolution-confidence/escalation-recommendation\n  engine (deterministic rule floor + LLM reasoning pass)\n- tools/resolution_tool.py — resolution_assess, escalate_ticket\n- tools/tickets.py — ticket_create/update/close\n- api/resolution.py — new REST endpoints (/api/v1/resolution/assess,\n  /escalate) so the dashboard''s buttons work without requiring voice\n\nBackend (additive changes, existing tools/features left as-is):\n- db/models.py: new Ticket model\n- core/session_state.py: sentiment_history + add_sentiment\n- core/events.py: sentiment model warmup at startup\n- pipeline/asr_worker.py: fire-and-forget sentiment scoring per customer\n  turn (customercare usecase only) → sentiment_update WS event\n- tools/registry.py, tools/policy.py: wire the 5 new tools in, permissioned\n  for csr/manager/operator/developer roles\n- services/front_llm.py, pipeline/front_llm.py: resolution/escalation\n  prompt guidance, keyword fast-paths, and arg schemas\n- contracts/ws_events.ts(+py): resolution_update, sentiment_update event\n  types and payload interfaces\n\nFrontend (new page, since no upstream UI existed for this):\n- components/ResolutionView.tsx: live sentiment meter, resolution\n  confidence/recommendation panel, KB citations, Assess Now / Create\n  Escalation Ticket buttons\n- components/transcript/ResolutionPageView.tsx: page wrapper (mirrors\n  PPTPageView.tsx)\n- store/types.ts, app.tsx, urlSync.ts, transcript/index.tsx, Sidebar.tsx,\n  MainDashboard.tsx, GuidelinePageView.tsx, helpers.tsx (isResolutionRelated):\n  wired \"resolution\" in as a first-class page/feature entry alongside PPT\n  Copilot and Trip Planner\n\nVerified: backend/main.py imports cleanly under backend/.venv; frontend\n`tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both pass clean.","tree":{"sha":"63c1d2aee25d5763d34d772219ccaa1d99826a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/63c1d2aee25d5763d34d772219ccaa1d99826a6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9","node_id":"C_kwDOTbOGdtoAKGYzNGZkZjNmMDllYjVjNjM5NDAzNGU4YmEwZGM3NWVhYTVjNzRkYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commit/3360c4d71b7c09f8e936b70e087bc7bfddbd2c8a","sha":"3360c4d71b7c09f8e936b70e087bc7bfddbd2c8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/3360c4d71b7c09f8e936b70e087bc7bfddbd2c8a"}],"sha":"f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/f34fdf3f09eb5c6394034e8ba0dc75eaa5c74dc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/commits/3360c4d71b7c09f8e936b70e087bc7bfddbd2c8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T16:19:46Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T16:19:46Z","email":"pagupta@griddynamics.com","name":"pagupta"},"message":"Comment out PILOT-native PPT Copilot, replace with upstream GD-template implementation\n\nDisables PILOT''s own PPT Copilot implementation (kept inline as commented-out\nreference) and swaps in the implementation from syugesh''s\npilot-voice-agent-backend (feature/ppt-copilot @ 869dd08d9) and\npilot-voice-agent-frontend (feature/ppt-view @ bba05b6a2):\n\n- backend/tools/ppt_copilot.py, backend/api/ppt.py,\n  backend/services/ppt_template_builder.py: old implementation commented out,\n  upstream implementation pasted in active with import paths rewritten to\n  PILOT''s `backend.` package prefix convention.\n- backend/tools/navigation.py: new file, upstream''s navigate_page tool for\n  voice-driven page redirects (\"take me to PPT Copilot\").\n- backend/data/ppt_templates/GD_template/: template assets the new\n  implementation depends on (gitignored, not committed).\n- registry.py, pipeline/front_llm.py, services/front_llm.py, tools/policy.py:\n  rewired to the new tool set — ppt_qa, ppt_create_slides,\n  ppt_clear_presentation, ppt_improvise_slide, ppt_save_slide, and route_page\n  no longer exist upstream and are commented out; route_page callers switched\n  to navigate_page.\n- core/session_state.py: added pending_add_slide, used by ppt_add_slide''s\n  \"what should the new slide be about?\" clarification flow.\n- services/agentic/subagents.py, tests/test_agentic.py: updated/disabled to\n  match (these files have no upstream equivalent — PILOT-only orchestration\n  layer, adapted in place rather than replaced).\n- frontend/src/components/PPTView.tsx: old implementation commented out,\n  upstream implementation (kind-aware editing, add-slide, 14 GD-template\n  slide kinds) pasted in active.\n- frontend/src/shared_voice.ts, contracts/ws_events.ts(.py): route_page WS\n  event/handler disabled, navigate_page added in its place.\n\nVerified: backend/tools/registry.py and backend/main.py import cleanly under\nbackend/.venv; frontend `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both pass clean.","tree":{"sha":"3345d68f040b6ff7f57008b21dcf14950d7a4dc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/trees/3345d68f040b6ff7f57008b21dcf14950d7a4dc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pawanguptapawan/PILOT_OS/git/commits/3360c4d71b7c09f8e936b70e087bc7bfddbd2c8a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256355312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pguptagrid","id":256355312,"login":"pguptagrid","node_id":"U_kgDOD0er8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pguptagrid/