/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/c75c0323b89d80a2a871902dfc50aae452ac8e6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T19:25:01Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T19:25:01Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat: Phase 9 — Helm chart updates & deployment infrastructure\n\n- Add SUPERSET_CHART_DIR env var to helmRenderer for configurable chart\n  template path (supports both local dev and in-cluster deployment)\n- Update BFF Containerfile to bundle Superset sub-chart templates and\n  use repo root as build context\n- Add env block to bff-deployment.yaml with SUPERSET_CHART_DIR\n- Add bff.chartDir to chart/values.yaml\n- Update plugin.yaml with Superset-specific description and RBAC\n  requirements for deployment operations\n- Update package.json description\n- Add Superset sub-chart values table, RBAC docs, and instance\n  deployment section to OPENSHIFT_DEPLOY.md\n- Add local Superset development guide to LOCAL_SETUP.md\n- Update helmRenderer tests for new chartDir validation\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e87983f3114709235683e8a004e4b1b887facd78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/e87983f3114709235683e8a004e4b1b887facd78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/c75c0323b89d80a2a871902dfc50aae452ac8e6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/c75c0323b89d80a2a871902dfc50aae452ac8e6b","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKGM3NWMwMzIzYjg5ZDgwYTJhODcxOTAyZGZjNTBhYWU0NTJhYzhlNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/984e2245fd538514ac1645c549ee8a32f897caab","sha":"984e2245fd538514ac1645c549ee8a32f897caab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/984e2245fd538514ac1645c549ee8a32f897caab"}],"sha":"c75c0323b89d80a2a871902dfc50aae452ac8e6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/c75c0323b89d80a2a871902dfc50aae452ac8e6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/984e2245fd538514ac1645c549ee8a32f897caab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T19:16:27Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T19:16:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 8 — Embedded Dashboards Page (#103)\n\n* feat: Phase 8 — Embedded Dashboards Page\n\nAdd @superset-ui/embedded-sdk dependency and implement the complete\nEmbedded Dashboards page with inline Superset dashboard viewing.\n\nHooks:\n- useSupersetDashboards: fetch dashboard list from BFF\n- useSupersetGuestToken: fetch guest token callback for SDK\n\nComponents:\n- DashboardList: PatternFly Card gallery with status labels\n- SupersetDashboardEmbed: wraps embedDashboard() SDK lifecycle\n\nPage:\n- EmbeddedDashboardsPage: replaces placeholder with full implementation\n  - List view: project selector, status guard, dashboard grid\n  - Embed view: toolbar with back/fullscreen/open-in-Superset, iframe embed\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix race condition in SupersetDashboardEmbed: track cancelled flag\n  so SDK unmount is called even if promise resolves after component\n  unmounts\n- Replace innerHTML with replaceChildren() for safer DOM cleanup\n- Add supersetDomain guard in embed view to show spinner until\n  Superset URL is available (prevents broken iframe on direct nav)\n- Extract inline styles to CSS classes (SupersetDashboardEmbed.css)\n- Fix setLoading(false) in useSupersetDashboards to not run after\n  abort\n- Remove isSelectable/isClickable from Card, disable button for\n  non-embeddable dashboards\n- Validate guestToken response shape in useSupersetGuestToken\n- Improve embed cleanup test to verify unmount is actually called\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(embed): add error handling for embedDashboard SDK failures (#109)\n\nAdd `.catch()` to the embedDashboard promise so SDK failures (network\nerrors, CORS issues, invalid domain) are caught and surfaced as a\nPatternFly danger Alert instead of triggering an unhandled promise\nrejection. The error state is cleared whenever the embedding deps\nchange, and the container div remains mounted at all times so the ref\nstays valid across error/recovery cycles.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dashboards): show not-running state instead of infinite spinner (#110)\n\nWhen navigating directly to an embedded dashboard URL while Superset is\nnot running, the status loads but status.url is undefined, making\nsupersetDomain falsy. This caused the combined `statusLoading || !supersetDomain`\nguard to keep showing a spinner forever with no way to escape.\n\nSplit the guard into two separate checks: one for the loading state (shows\nspinner) and one for the not-running/no-domain state (shows NotRunningState\nwith a link to Instance Management). Adds four new tests covering these\ncases in the Embed view.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(routes): extract navigate paths to shared route constants (#111)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(css): move fullscreen overlay styles to page-level CSS (#112)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(css): make fullscreen embed fill available viewport space (#113)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d55b0dd34436159957b79fb1c324c7d9c324284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/9d55b0dd34436159957b79fb1c324c7d9c324284"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/984e2245fd538514ac1645c549ee8a32f897caab","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d55b0dd34436159957b79fb1c324c7d9c324284\nparent a08779a3f19ff7d262453e4ce18f81b3c5534404\nparent ed032948177487c505acc0a3ae8e57d3626036bf\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784402187 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784402187 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 8 — Embedded Dashboards Page (#103)\n\n* feat: Phase 8 — Embedded Dashboards Page\n\nAdd @superset-ui/embedded-sdk dependency and implement the complete\nEmbedded Dashboards page with inline Superset dashboard viewing.\n\nHooks:\n- useSupersetDashboards: fetch dashboard list from BFF\n- useSupersetGuestToken: fetch guest token callback for SDK\n\nComponents:\n- DashboardList: PatternFly Card gallery with status labels\n- SupersetDashboardEmbed: wraps embedDashboard() SDK lifecycle\n\nPage:\n- EmbeddedDashboardsPage: replaces placeholder with full implementation\n  - List view: project selector, status guard, dashboard grid\n  - Embed view: toolbar with back/fullscreen/open-in-Superset, iframe embed\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix race condition in SupersetDashboardEmbed: track cancelled flag\n  so SDK unmount is called even if promise resolves after component\n  unmounts\n- Replace innerHTML with replaceChildren() for safer DOM cleanup\n- Add supersetDomain guard in embed view to show spinner until\n  Superset URL is available (prevents broken iframe on direct nav)\n- Extract inline styles to CSS classes (SupersetDashboardEmbed.css)\n- Fix setLoading(false) in useSupersetDashboards to not run after\n  abort\n- Remove isSelectable/isClickable from Card, disable button for\n  non-embeddable dashboards\n- Validate guestToken response shape in useSupersetGuestToken\n- Improve embed cleanup test to verify unmount is actually called\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(embed): add error handling for embedDashboard SDK failures (#109)\n\nAdd `.catch()` to the embedDashboard promise so SDK failures (network\nerrors, CORS issues, invalid domain) are caught and surfaced as a\nPatternFly danger Alert instead of triggering an unhandled promise\nrejection. The error state is cleared whenever the embedding deps\nchange, and the container div remains mounted at all times so the ref\nstays valid across error/recovery cycles.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dashboards): show not-running state instead of infinite spinner (#110)\n\nWhen navigating directly to an embedded dashboard URL while Superset is\nnot running, the status loads but status.url is undefined, making\nsupersetDomain falsy. This caused the combined `statusLoading || !supersetDomain`\nguard to keep showing a spinner forever with no way to escape.\n\nSplit the guard into two separate checks: one for the loading state (shows\nspinner) and one for the not-running/no-domain state (shows NotRunningState\nwith a link to Instance Management). Adds four new tests covering these\ncases in the Embed view.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(routes): extract navigate paths to shared route constants (#111)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(css): move fullscreen overlay styles to page-level CSS (#112)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(css): make fullscreen embed fill available viewport space (#113)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW9ELCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8q8QAJh3raIEjC9uAYt8Qe4O0Y6U\n1uS8f7YQMLIbB/aM1yk+yx5aLw3I9ys9cVF8/WwdmTACCjkf6CeBLcDJLZ5PUE4e\niaXDNTCRkxsF+EEbE99TsvwBFgfYdvtc5/T/7H0uwsvPJiWeEUUJoV8tC1UXxvE1\nQ1+R/lYH/OMjLpADfVq6bg9B2JZstmELyExG8w81KcjN3moqM96gty4A7XKBOZaw\n2pEK4Ay3SyrDE7C2qiwKhGq5x4OZzB+saT9cz8t1OTr104waYd14COLc8HPyCg1W\nuWM+bxkfajM4SLOeLmSDZb1mI3LR+hFLwgyVv0GIR4UHClxsZJ1cCo7sD9kOns6h\nnkplStLWmUo3Yoo8xEvnN0YWT9xT1jh2U5823G+886DOAOKCQ/t1SmEZoB2jvSV7\nXvyjS2jg12dm5HxJ7KLPTMkdJZg/L7r7d29OBD7TrrnvI8Zp/gUsJpAjSoNkNDlC\nqWbK5l518na4ft2/w/nLvRrtz2bfr/hpGRJ8I/m7OfiyOz47qWMkxxwtjPTIAw2P\nBGkvYDH0JXWBF2wpwD6zG9hmoP48TkYURPRUIqIXCUmwSoEHGe+4iIrXft9mo7+F\nibwPbA1//mNotyfd2BjUI9oavqj5yGB/8Ar+gC2s4pA0HVExGH+fzmpmcBdaXl2w\nl7f5XioXAicwEQp3bPk0\n=UD0Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T19:16:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users