followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/27e28811b7e7c4616529b2e8e183a844ab820138/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T18:16:19Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T18:16:19Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat: Phase 8 — Embedded Dashboards Page\n\nAdd @superset-ui/embedded-sdk dependency and implement the complete\nEmbedded Dashboards page with inline Superset dashboard viewing.\n\nHooks:\n- useSupersetDashboards: fetch dashboard list from BFF\n- useSupersetGuestToken: fetch guest token callback for SDK\n\nComponents:\n- DashboardList: PatternFly Card gallery with status labels\n- SupersetDashboardEmbed: wraps embedDashboard() SDK lifecycle\n\nPage:\n- EmbeddedDashboardsPage: replaces placeholder with full implementation\n  - List view: project selector, status guard, dashboard grid\n  - Embed view: toolbar with back/fullscreen/open-in-Superset, iframe embed\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8967c047624df6e62dafa066429fa050606941d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/d8967c047624df6e62dafa066429fa050606941d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/27e28811b7e7c4616529b2e8e183a844ab820138","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/27e28811b7e7c4616529b2e8e183a844ab820138","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKDI3ZTI4ODExYjdlN2M0NjE2NTI5YjJlOGUxODNhODQ0YWI4MjAxMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/a08779a3f19ff7d262453e4ce18f81b3c5534404","sha":"a08779a3f19ff7d262453e4ce18f81b3c5534404","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/a08779a3f19ff7d262453e4ce18f81b3c5534404"}],"sha":"27e28811b7e7c4616529b2e8e183a844ab820138","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/27e28811b7e7c4616529b2e8e183a844ab820138"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/a08779a3f19ff7d262453e4ce18f81b3c5534404/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T16:40:34Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T16:40:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 7 — Instance Management Page (#88)\n\n* feat: add Instance Management page with deploy/monitor/teardown lifecycle\n\nPhase 7 implementation — replaces the placeholder InstanceManagementPage with\na fully functional deploy/status/teardown lifecycle UI:\n\n- src/app/types.ts: frontend type definitions (SupersetStatus, DeployResult, etc.)\n- useSupersetDeployment hook: POST deploy, DELETE teardown via BFF\n- useSupersetStatus hook: polling with adaptive interval (10s active, 30s stable)\n- DeploymentStatusCard: four-state display (not-deployed, deploying, running, error)\n- DeployForm: project selector, RBAC permission check, confirmation modal\n- InstanceManagementPage: wires all hooks and components with teardown modal\n- Full test coverage for all hooks, components, and page\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix stale closure over `status` in useSupersetStatus polling — use\n  hasDataRef instead of closing over state variable\n- Fix refresh racing with polling — refresh now resets the poll cycle\n  (clears timer, aborts in-flight request, restarts)\n- Remove dual error channels in useSupersetDeployment — return undefined\n  on error instead of re-throwing; callers check return value\n- Lift project selection state to InstanceManagementPage — DeployForm\n  receives selectedProject/onProjectSelect as props to keep parent and\n  child in sync\n- Remove non-null assertion on selectedProject in retry handler — use\n  guard check instead\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deploy): guard hasRequiredPermissions against empty create-verb results (#95)\n\nArray.every() on an empty array returns true (vacuous truth). When no\ncreate-verb RBAC results exist, hasRequiredPermissions previously\nreturned true, incorrectly enabling the Deploy button.\n\nAdd a createResults.length > 0 guard so the function only returns true\nwhen at least one create-verb result is present and all are allowed.\nAdd a regression test covering the vacuous truth edge case.\n\nCloses #89\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hooks): abort refresh controller in useSupersetStatus cleanup (#96)\n\nThe useEffect cleanup was aborting the `controller` variable captured\nin the effect closure. When `refresh()` creates a new AbortController\nand stores it in `controllerRef.current`, the cleanup no longer targets\nthe active controller, so any in-flight fetch started by refresh() is\nnot cancelled on unmount.\n\nFix: replace `controller.abort()` with `controllerRef.current?.abort()`\nin the cleanup function so it always targets the latest active controller.\n\nAdds a test to verify that unmounting after refresh() aborts the refresh\ncontroller rather than the stale closure-captured one.\n\nCloses #91\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): add retry feedback and deployError display to DeploymentStatusCard (#97)\n\n* fix(ui): add retry feedback and deployError display to DeploymentStatusCard\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ui): add tests for retry loading and deployError display in DeploymentStatusCard\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): validate status.url before rendering as href (#98)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ui): add retry-from-error test and fix teardown test scoping (#99)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): replace inline styles with PatternFly utility classes in DeploymentStatusCard (#100)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): rename misleading \"Retry failed\" alert title to \"Deploy request failed\" (#101)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c3714c4d28a64e626a2f74988f8690b46a7fa9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/8c3714c4d28a64e626a2f74988f8690b46a7fa9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/a08779a3f19ff7d262453e4ce18f81b3c5534404","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c3714c4d28a64e626a2f74988f8690b46a7fa9c\nparent ceb30932e99c060c8d16c6a3f215ec20ec2e5589\nparent db1e26b7f42c8d995115231c3b36156d27a860bb\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784392834 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784392834 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 7 — Instance Management Page (#88)\n\n* feat: add Instance Management page with deploy/monitor/teardown lifecycle\n\nPhase 7 implementation — replaces the placeholder InstanceManagementPage with\na fully functional deploy/status/teardown lifecycle UI:\n\n- src/app/types.ts: frontend type definitions (SupersetStatus, DeployResult, etc.)\n- useSupersetDeployment hook: POST deploy, DELETE teardown via BFF\n- useSupersetStatus hook: polling with adaptive interval (10s active, 30s stable)\n- DeploymentStatusCard: four-state display (not-deployed, deploying, running, error)\n- DeployForm: project selector, RBAC permission check, confirmation modal\n- InstanceManagementPage: wires all hooks and components with teardown modal\n- Full test coverage for all hooks, components, and page\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix stale closure over `status` in useSupersetStatus polling — use\n  hasDataRef instead of closing over state variable\n- Fix refresh racing with polling — refresh now resets the poll cycle\n  (clears timer, aborts in-flight request, restarts)\n- Remove dual error channels in useSupersetDeployment — return undefined\n  on error instead of re-throwing; callers check return value\n- Lift project selection state to InstanceManagementPage — DeployForm\n  receives selectedProject/onProjectSelect as props to keep parent and\n  child in sync\n- Remove non-null assertion on selectedProject in retry handler — use\n  guard check instead\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deploy): guard hasRequiredPermissions against empty create-verb results (#95)\n\nArray.every() on an empty array returns true (vacuous truth). When no\ncreate-verb RBAC results exist, hasRequiredPermissions previously\nreturned true, incorrectly enabling the Deploy button.\n\nAdd a createResults.length > 0 guard so the function only returns true\nwhen at least one create-verb result is present and all are allowed.\nAdd a regression test covering the vacuous truth edge case.\n\nCloses #89\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hooks): abort refresh controller in useSupersetStatus cleanup (#96)\n\nThe useEffect cleanup was aborting the `controller` variable captured\nin the effect closure. When `refresh()` creates a new AbortController\nand stores it in `controllerRef.current`, the cleanup no longer targets\nthe active controller, so any in-flight fetch started by refresh() is\nnot cancelled on unmount.\n\nFix: replace `controller.abort()` with `controllerRef.current?.abort()`\nin the cleanup function so it always targets the latest active controller.\n\nAdds a test to verify that unmounting after refresh() aborts the refresh\ncontroller rather than the stale closure-captured one.\n\nCloses #91\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): add retry feedback and deployError display to DeploymentStatusCard (#97)\n\n* fix(ui): add retry feedback and deployError display to DeploymentStatusCard\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ui): add tests for retry loading and deployError display in DeploymentStatusCard\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): validate status.url before rendering as href (#98)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(ui): add retry-from-error test and fix teardown test scoping (#99)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): replace inline styles with PatternFly utility classes in DeploymentStatusCard (#100)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): rename misleading \"Retry failed\" alert title to \"Deploy request failed\" (#101)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW6yCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg5QQAItk80znLPcHLG18mqUThqZN\nJfKobbG2wLMHA0P1lYVaYzDtsnLtwOheQH2PaSgjl9MLT7MONEk6J+J2V68cPf2w\nWD/48krVBVNeOyKSs7Z/WOW5UYYZulPWrxAHRhCED9payOeaUg3Ka+SBIGHf4tGQ\nV7M9AWnc2UHc7EduvQYVm3O3Gb0Nr1vI+WVgSL/0+iB36q4O1u1Avn1ujUWXf/fp\njBx6GT0bmKG9qC6L1PJra4GxzU/i8/4mC5unhyDt4YQtWbogTx7Hn7DXSLJcUKnW\ndAaX3cO+26+cpE8dCSJmzpmWr2v0WrLul8Hn/M2uXhdadN4iv4MWimyYpRNwLDLT\njmnhp0WcKvxVbdGzTOWy19bu30aTuaj+Fx8mGrPJCTfme5yHVfrD6OssBkgSSQUu\ngUmqBN/8Oqat10H37CGm/0t1BmYR2kMMd5m1X/kM772EuM+QtcT9NNw