flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/1766ce92976325b234b7e2a096be2e6337c36e13","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKDE3NjZjZTkyOTc2MzI1YjIzNGI3ZTJhMDk2YmUyZTYzMzdjMzZlMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3","sha":"be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3"}],"sha":"1766ce92976325b234b7e2a096be2e6337c36e13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/1766ce92976325b234b7e2a096be2e6337c36e13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T16:13:29Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T16:13:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(hooks): abort refresh controller in useSupersetStatus cleanup (#96)\n\nThe useEffect cleanup was aborting the `controller` variable captured\nin the effect closure. When `refresh()` creates a new AbortController\nand stores it in `controllerRef.current`, the cleanup no longer targets\nthe active controller, so any in-flight fetch started by refresh() is\nnot cancelled on unmount.\n\nFix: replace `controller.abort()` with `controllerRef.current?.abort()`\nin the cleanup function so it always targets the latest active controller.\n\nAdds a test to verify that unmounting after refresh() aborts the refresh\ncontroller rather than the stale closure-captured one.\n\nCloses #91\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8a743f3abf8e5f2fcc02db200a923a1f7043439","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/d8a743f3abf8e5f2fcc02db200a923a1f7043439"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3","verification":{"payload":"tree d8a743f3abf8e5f2fcc02db200a923a1f7043439\nparent 175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784391209 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784391209 -0400\n\nfix(hooks): abort refresh controller in useSupersetStatus cleanup (#96)\n\nThe useEffect cleanup was aborting the `controller` variable captured\nin the effect closure. When `refresh()` creates a new AbortController\nand stores it in `controllerRef.current`, the cleanup no longer targets\nthe active controller, so any in-flight fetch started by refresh() is\nnot cancelled on unmount.\n\nFix: replace `controller.abort()` with `controllerRef.current?.abort()`\nin the cleanup function so it always targets the latest active controller.\n\nAdds a test to verify that unmounting after refresh() aborts the refresh\ncontroller rather than the stale closure-captured one.\n\nCloses #91\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW6YqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADhoQAIe6Ddcx8ccEKMFjYKm1USUg\nucz3gNHmMsRjSTWV2tFnR+7h0yYSkueD7vqkAhJshpbtUDxknQiXs0Z1lWaw96J5\nYjS368wMsIdVksU5LNcpgqn4OtwYFYhY+mvv1vK934n5SXTa7qe+ehvrIvnegMg+\nFzqLKcR7sIJdA1vDkdQRPj9wew0f9GK1sZ+u4b0nGHXdbH2wy8TKUayYrEP65OFa\n8POuZCnA77D5R6psUrY7GbmwgsEiP9Z4qtMORR9cJkHsoi2BaENAL4qk+hbsue+z\niGKlDj7j/hKqeLSInGUfAIB4nFw7RulFUC8o6DjrpmlZglXdjc2904tb97dKVpDi\n6T5pQvr776eDDFWL0oT86gVtTnaAMCbsMWMpdl7bPggbDIG2uTroMDgMG84fUWgN\nGRIyPJXpUkL272MgQAOyNhOTPH18u8e7RH4xxoCH5lLh/u3PXAjoS+TLvmg9Wb9F\nUpxY2INQ1vmP8L5c9K5SbK2hXwRG8Vhiw7vGXLZ4TirEdmgc9QGkBP5kOCg4i2M3\nxIp1j1AhHN4tLV8fRqZSltsS+7SaCfp3THSV13VeqC9uvJWHrJ8e00Dc+YWZ0iT1\n4tD25rBa0zbq56Wu329SfsSyprhWgWq+Rb3zs/ARRSYC7bf+uJSxDrmMOs9pKMbh\nqxePoM2FC7wh+mPqOSig\n=vZnL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T16:13:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKGJlNmZlMjg2NWMzODc1M2MwYWY5YjI2ODNiMTkwODgzNGNjODE3ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0","sha":"175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0"}],"sha":"be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/be6fe2865c38753c0af9b2683b1908834cc817e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T16:13:27Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T16:13:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): guard hasRequiredPermissions against empty create-verb results (#95)\n\nArray.every() on an empty array returns true (vacuous truth). When no\ncreate-verb RBAC results exist, hasRequiredPermissions previously\nreturned true, incorrectly enabling the Deploy button.\n\nAdd a createResults.length > 0 guard so the function only returns true\nwhen at least one create-verb result is present and all are allowed.\nAdd a regression test covering the vacuous truth edge case.\n\nCloses #89\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f88ba986deca92e19371bfdbca616b3882232e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/6f88ba986deca92e19371bfdbca616b3882232e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f88ba986deca92e19371bfdbca616b3882232e3\nparent ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784391207 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784391207 -0400\n\nfix(deploy): guard hasRequiredPermissions against empty create-verb results (#95)\n\nArray.every() on an empty array returns true (vacuous truth). When no\ncreate-verb RBAC results exist, hasRequiredPermissions previously\nreturned true, incorrectly enabling the Deploy button.\n\nAdd a createResults.length > 0 guard so the function only returns true\nwhen at least one create-verb result is present and all are allowed.\nAdd a regression test covering the vacuous truth edge case.\n\nCloses #89\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW6YnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEpoQAHWjyuBeIyOiOXrcPWnXI6jf\nfvMFHxCU5d4/R+jo+YpupuZ2fDSaPIKTw8A0lvbyeApzWeZYezHQol65JRIev7tK\nqjNpQh6zCxc2v1zXYPK8UGA1CVKAA7nf/t+351S3KWOENyLf5q3aOBnW+9Z7BQTL\nn0GWKe1elkGhPjnb7X5+s/8BdmPxXRp+qkHFmP/5lwLXUv6vC4S6B5lL8pfnsiqn\njYCCGQDTeBUuNXuRZ19wge64BVC0c8amNa86py72ScHBO2IUiQLSAR4eejN4ojtS\ndsL/MgpQ5KfFSYK3AyGmjJY+nKpP6B8Izns+jU9Kd8r/74w4U+c1z9rHmJCvDJwh\nRoIL21ZTBlVB1Is4pe00NqWhoCNHqTh6ikp+6Ca6broAO4bEXLtm5bsgfQodhLTW\nAdJz1m6p+dC4mtKxR0p4pzKSwcYovwWKE9lLdta0x9d2YhzoYj0TZmRpZUMXDSLy\nTuIEes6TD+v3XPl9x64c+9jwZuARkk/QdtrzDb0RLwOKnqalJ1Vb5h/Izkyxpgvo\n7JLLQc6W3M34kWgluMHcDYMv9hK0F9kbMVTAbINUoEDhuKncqFXnQ529xwQGcP6Y\niekOJfw3szl0XoZ2Tlap6e7xpeqWe5jlEpPecH8CS52yYKA5U6be5ZgNXc0DpzqG\nmZoPSNrrZjOWlJmltuJ4\n=x8PI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T16:13:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKDE3NWFkNDI4YjBiMzViYjJlYTMzNDhhMjgwNWY2MjZlOTBiYzNiYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137","sha":"ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137"}],"sha":"175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/175ad428b0b35bb2ea3348a2805f626e90bc3ba0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T15:57:44Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T15:57:44Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix stale closure over `status` in useSupersetStatus polling — use\n  hasDataRef instead of closing over state variable\n- Fix refresh racing with polling — refresh now resets the poll cycle\n  (clears timer, aborts in-flight request, restarts)\n- Remove dual error channels in useSupersetDeployment — return undefined\n  on error instead of re-throwing; callers check return value\n- Lift project selection state to InstanceManagementPage — DeployForm\n  receives selectedProject/onProjectSelect as props to keep parent and\n  child in sync\n- Remove non-null assertion on selectedProject in retry handler — use\n  guard check instead\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e1122d4fb08d17dd215501d2d405cae80380cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/3e1122d4fb08d17dd215501d2d405cae80380cb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKGZmYjY5YTkyNDZiNWQzMTEyOTYxOTU3OTVmMzQ2MWVjNGE0ZWIxMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f","sha":"46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f"}],"sha":"ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/ffb69a9246b5d311296195795f3461ec4a4eb137"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T15:53:21Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T15:53:21Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat: add Instance Management page with deploy/monitor/teardown lifecycle\n\nPhase 7 implementation — replaces the placeholder InstanceManagementPage with\na fully functional deploy/status/teardown lifecycle UI:\n\n- src/app/types.ts: frontend type definitions (SupersetStatus, DeployResult, etc.)\n- useSupersetDeployment hook: POST deploy, DELETE teardown via BFF\n- useSupersetStatus hook: polling with adaptive interval (10s active, 30s stable)\n- DeploymentStatusCard: four-state display (not-deployed, deploying, running, error)\n- DeployForm: project selector, RBAC permission check, confirmation modal\n- InstanceManagementPage: wires all hooks and components with teardown modal\n- Full test coverage for all hooks, components, and page\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b4bc6f4630c933563f50b73628104c1238ad160","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/3b4bc6f4630c933563f50b73628104c1238ad160"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKDQ2YWQyOTQzN2YzZWJiMjgyMzQ4MDUzMTBlNDc3NGQxZjM4ODZiNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/ceb30932e99c060c8d16c6a3f215ec20ec2e5589","sha":"ceb30932e99c060c8d16c6a3f215ec20ec2e5589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/ceb30932e99c060c8d16c6a3f215ec20ec2e5589"}],"sha":"46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/46ad29437f3ebb28234805310e4774d1f3886b4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/ceb30932e99c060c8d16c6a3f215ec20ec2e5589/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T15:41:25Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T15:41:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(bff): Phase 6 — Guest Token & Dashboard Listing Endpoints (#77)\n\n* feat(bff): Phase 6 — Guest Token & Dashboard Listing Endpoints\n\nAdd BFF endpoints for embedding Superset dashboards:\n\n- GET /api/superset/guest-token — generates scoped guest tokens for\n  embedded dashboard access, mapping RHOAI user identity to Superset\n  guest user via OpenShift User API\n- GET /api/superset/dashboards — lists dashboards from Superset API\n  with pagination support\n\nNew utilities:\n- secretReader: reads admin credentials and resolves Superset URL from\n  K8s Secret and Route resources\n- userIdentity: extracts authenticated user info from OpenShift API\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): separate credential and identity error handling in guest token route\n\nRestructure the guest token route to handle getAdminCredentials and\ngetUserInfo errors independently. Previously both ran in Promise.all\nand shared a catch block, which meant a 404 from the OpenShift User\nAPI could be misidentified as \"Superset instance not found\".\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Clamp negative page values to 0 and handle pageSize=0 correctly\n- Stop forwarding internal Superset API paths in error responses;\n  log details server-side, return generic message to clients\n- Throw on missing metadata.name instead of silently defaulting to\n  ''unknown'' — prevents creating guest tokens for a placeholder identity\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(bff): add test for getUserInfo failure in guest-token route (#84)\n\nCovers the case where getUserInfo throws a K8sApiError (e.g., 403 from\nthe OpenShift User API), verifying the generic catch block returns 500\nwith the expected error message.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(bff): remove unused getSupersetUrl export (#83)\n\n* chore(bff): remove unused getSupersetUrl export\n\nRemove the `export` keyword from `getSupersetUrl` in secretReader.ts so\nit is no longer part of the module''s public API. Refactor\n`getAdminCredentials` to call the internal helper instead of duplicating\nthe Route-then-service URL resolution inline. Add a JSDoc-style comment\ndocumenting the function''s purpose and its reservation for future\ncredential-free URL lookups (e.g. a lightweight status endpoint).\n\nRemove the now-redundant `getSupersetUrl` describe block and its import\nfrom the test file; URL resolution behaviour continues to be covered\nindirectly through the `getAdminCredentials` tests.\n\nCloses #78\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings (round 1)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(bff): surface user-identity errors in guest-token route (#85)\n\nCatch K8sApiError from getUserInfo specifically and return the upstream\nstatus code with a descriptive \"Unable to resolve user identity\" message,\nrather than falling through to the generic 500 handler. This makes it\neasier to distinguish identity-resolution failures (e.g. 403 when the\nuser''s token lacks permission to call the OpenShift User API) from\nunrelated server errors.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(bff): parallelize getAdminCredentials and getUserInfo in guest-token route (#86)\n\nRun both independent K8s calls concurrently via Promise.allSettled to\nreduce latency in the guest-token endpoint.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(bff): extract shared status-clamping and UUID validation helpers (#87)\n\n- Add `safeHttpStatus(code)` to routeHelpers.ts — clamps upstream HTTP\n  status codes to 400-599, defaulting to 502 for out-of-range values\n- Add `isValidUuid(value)` to resourceNames.ts — centralises RFC 4122\n  UUID validation alongside the existing namespace validator\n- Remove the local UUID_REGEX constant from supersetGuestToken.ts\n- Replace inline clamping expressions in supersetGuestToken.ts and\n  supersetDashboards.ts with calls to safeHttpStatus\n- Add unit tests for both helpers (28 new tests across two new files)\n\nCloses #82\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae8636ca74491bc332c966ed4897a1d0c6bc93ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/ae8636ca74491bc332c966ed4897a1d0c6bc93ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/ceb30932e99c060c8d16c6a3f215ec20ec2e5589","verification":{"payload":"tree ae8636ca74491bc332c966ed4897a1d0c6bc93ca\nparent f81c73a47f3a67ae046cb764e0ff3235f1d226b6\nparent 74eee0523e60947af6c0c26671f3bceee34152b6\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784389285 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784389285 -0400\n\nfeat(bff): Phase 6 — Guest Token & Dashboard Listing Endpoints (#77)\n\n* feat(bff): Phase 6 — Guest Token & Dashboard Listing Endpoints\n\nAdd BFF endpoints for embedding Superset dashboards:\n\n- GET /api/superset/guest-token — generates scoped guest tokens for\n  embedded dashboard access, mapping RHOAI user identity to Superset\n  guest user via OpenShift User API\n- GET /api/superset/dashboards — lists dashboards from Superset API\n  with pagination support\n\nNew utilities:\n- secretReader: reads admin credentials and resolves Superset URL from\n  K8s Secret and Route resources\n- userIdentity: extracts authenticated user info from OpenShift API\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): separate credential and identity error handling in guest token route\n\nRestructure the guest token route to handle getAdminCredentials and\ngetUserInfo errors independently. Previously both ran in Promise.all\nand shared a catch block, which meant a 404 from the OpenShift User\nAPI could be misidentified as \"Superset instance not found\".\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Clamp negative page values to 0 and handle pageSize=0 correctly\n- Stop forwarding internal Superset API paths in error responses;\n  log details server-side, return generic message to clients\n- Throw on missing metadata.name instead of silently defaulting to\n  ''unknown'' — prevents creating guest tokens for a placeholder identity\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(bff): add test for getUserInfo failure in guest-token route (#84)\n\nCovers the case where getUserInfo throws a K8sApiError (e.g., 403 from\nthe OpenShift User API), verifying the generic catch block returns 500\nwith the expected error message.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(bff): remove unused getSupersetUrl export (#83)\n\n* chore(bff): remove unused getSupersetUrl export\n\nRemove the `export` keyword from `getSupersetUrl` in secretReader.ts so\nit is no longer part of the module''s public API. Refactor\n`getAdminCredentials` to call the internal helper instead of duplicating\nthe Route-then-service URL resolution inline. Add a JSDoc-style comment\ndocumenting the function''s purpose and its reservation for future\ncredential-free URL lookups (e.g. a lightweight status endpoint).\n\nRemove the now-redundant `getSupersetUrl` describe block and its import\nfrom the test file; URL resolution behaviour continues to be covered\nindirectly through the `getAdminCredentials` tests.\n\nCloses #78\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings (round 1)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(bff): surface user-identity errors in guest-token route (#85)\n\nCatch K8sApiError from getUserInfo specifically and return the upstream\nstatus code with a descriptive \"Unable to resolve user identity\" message,\nrather than falling through to the generic 500 handler. This makes it\neasier to distinguish identity-resolution failures (e.g. 403 when the\nuser''s token lacks permission to call the OpenShift User API) from\nunrelated server errors.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(bff): parallelize getAdminCredentials and getUserInfo in guest-token route (#86)\n\nRun both independent K8s calls concurrently via Promise.allSettled to\nreduce latency in the guest-token endpoint.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(bff): extract shared status-clamping and UUID validation helpers (#87)\n\n- Add `safeHttpStatus(code)` to routeHelpers.ts — clamps upstream HTTP\n  status codes to 400-599, defaulting to 502 for out-of-range values\n- Add `isValidUuid(value)` to resourceNames.ts — centralises RFC 4122\n  UUID validation alongside the existing namespace validator\n- Remove the local UUID_REGEX constant from supersetGuestToken.ts\n- Replace inline clamping expressions in supersetGuestToken.ts and\n  supersetDashboards.ts with calls to safeHttpStatus\n- Add unit tests for both helpers (28 new tests across two new files)\n\nCloses #82\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW56lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEhoQAGAqnGUot1dLvOFEhcX4IKFn\nW6zQy0w5xE//uz/wMFA8ZHKReib57XxRhTan9KoxKGPV8W5PjfGC48uN7I1oCKQd\nIldLDK5vhCCwdHzkJ7iY3bU/K9/Fs0YGxeHktJqLvMY5ufBtxf11m2MBAKTAK/Yu\nBKtLRwPZgh4OFlnfIRqraa5a/VicVYvY6kl9PRfeqkkE5rTiwNdcfYegGruJuLLJ\nbfsRrK3bu2DDyMIbQMCrSNZgWyE9pQWyWedEQIw3Ya/Fo457aeMUOZu/bclteTYU\nBu5iwg0Az8EI7d/Kb26SCIztfnuDVMfe8I9EBulKe8nufokGebZSecrYpsUag/J2\nbg4tFuwuY32rGQwojmk5kAFIu8NK5fJmk5ZOGmLLvmN6/0zYNt27d/M0d