/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/7877e7ee86d7ea1e7c86e8fe7bec627e05eac89d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:30:13Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:30:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): replace req.token! assertions with runtime guards (#74)\n\nIntroduce requireToken() helper in bff/src/utils/routeHelpers.ts that\nreturns the token or sends a 401 JSON response and returns null. Replace\nall three req.token! non-null assertions in supersetDeploy, supersetStatus,\nand supersetConfig routes with this guard so TypeScript can no longer mask\naccidental middleware omissions at compile time.\n\nAdd a missing-token test case to each route test suite (POST /deploy,\nDELETE /deploy, GET /status, GET /config) that mounts the router without\nauth middleware and asserts a 401 response with { error: ''Authentication\nrequired'' }.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c95f5c3230ecda65a891df4e54c3a69fed825ec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/c95f5c3230ecda65a891df4e54c3a69fed825ec4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/7877e7ee86d7ea1e7c86e8fe7bec627e05eac89d","verification":{"payload":"tree c95f5c3230ecda65a891df4e54c3a69fed825ec4\nparent d64e656233f275bb67232a0adb5cc2334ca019b