/commits/8fb3d011ab5831b981d70bac8b69d049ce9afdcb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/41c424ebaa4911898a37194b3e017bcf051496b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:07:12Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:07:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): read APP_VERSION from chart metadata instead of hardcoding (#68)\n\n* fix(bff): read APP_VERSION from chart metadata instead of hardcoding\n\nReplace the hardcoded APP_VERSION constant in supersetConfig.ts with a\ncall to loadChartMeta(DEFAULT_CHART_DIR).appVersion so the version\nreturned by /api/superset/config always matches chart/charts/superset/\nChart.yaml and never silently drifts when the chart appVersion is bumped.\n\nExport loadChartMeta and DEFAULT_CHART_DIR from helmRenderer.ts to make\nthem available outside of that module. Update the supersetConfig test to\nmock helmRenderer with a sentinel version (99.0.0-test) that proves the\nroute reads its version from chart metadata rather than a literal string.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): add fallback for APP_VERSION when chart directory is unavailable\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8540bd95b39561abe7f1def36a369b230a12b43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/c8540bd95b39561abe7f1def36a369b230a12b43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/41c424ebaa4911898a37194b3e017bcf051496b9","verification":{"payload":"tree c8540bd95b39561abe7f1def36a369b230a12b43\nparent bdd0b623a42c055d422631aa71cc634fb811df23\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784380032 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784380032 -0400\n\nfix(bff): read APP_VERSION from chart metadata instead of hardcoding (#68)\n\n* fix(bff): read APP_VERSION from chart metadata instead of hardcoding\n\nReplace the hardcoded APP_VERSION constant in supersetConfig.ts with a\ncall to loadChartMeta(DEFAULT_CHART_DIR).appVersion so the version\nreturned by /api/superset/config always matches chart/charts/superset/\nChart.yaml and never silently drifts when the chart appVersion is bumped.\n\nExport loadChartMeta and DEFAULT_CHART_DIR from helmRenderer.ts to make\nthem available outside of that module. Update the supersetConfig test to\nmock helmRenderer with a sentinel version (99.0.0-test) that proves the\nroute reads its version from chart metadata rather than a literal string.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): add fallback for APP_VERSION when chart directory is unavailable\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW3qACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi10QAKnn5KBKxPRsVad9OOMdPuxM\nqgaKS1DCYNjmTQ3RBRt4u7wZtgmzUpQoaiM7OVOiHdxII9yRt3tc/rf4tW84Bc2w\nbLjxQZfs/js+4nde1n1kTBHc11yAttnUQTgBCajbVsi2EX/gGrWm8ZaGClpef9VH\ngxOYEKiGPzbJ9iRGgMAJYV4FD3iyLt5JjiV2qAQsu8Cm/6yEHLgcC53z4thQTPi8\nit1PhAvqWLOTlrH/X8glK5sMH1ST8+jsGs5INiI+HCOwZeMmbGlAixLw2iv9Kciz\nx0Fnpt8i76nBVjw0pUj7hexsEcmpyA4jkOtkNMY7rW0tAklU2iGpRsX//pARjp8n\nMdn5F/g4Rlv5NQOLQ2qw1WElPK2f8Yts5fjAJFxGKHmuVx0LelQd0I4siaeHp6PR\nsCGOiNzo6WpWyvYZvnomYOwKELmOcxDT+wN1GnVvH5T+amIYRlC43J9kULhApqds\nawovyxCjfCIff57d8ceVkJRGy5KAMoj7IR0+s2KLtf9LNMvCNlQZsU/kZS2N4dLw\nRIyLgfTXicSr/o/KNOQre8LbVnUjEzdHbedFE4Dd/HQN+iFLO7QJHab1eUnntaIl\n8masnvgL5AJcbnLd0rRK3f4K+1hEl2Gqn5KN849WXGLPeJfJpihcpMzlBfLJaGPk\nawTx1Qdpf7VnkqwVqJnZ\n=EWfr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T13:07:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/41c424ebaa4911898a37194b3e017bcf051496b9","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKDQxYzQyNGViYWE0OTExODk4YTM3MTk0YjNlMDE3YmNmMDUxNDk2Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/bdd0b623a42c055d422631aa71cc634fb811df23","sha":"bdd0b623a42c055d422631aa71cc634fb811df23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/bdd0b623a42c055d422631aa71cc634fb811df23"}],"sha":"41c424ebaa4911898a37194b3e017bcf051496b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/41c424ebaa4911898a37194b3e017bcf051496b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/bdd0b623a42c055d422631aa71cc634fb811df23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:00:33Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:00:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): sanitize K8sApiError body in Express error handler (#67)\n\n* fix(bff): sanitize K8sApiError body in Express error handler\n\n- Remove raw K8s response body from K8sApiError.message so it is never\n  accidentally forwarded to clients via err.message (e.g., in route-level\n  error arrays). The body is still available via err.body for server-side\n  programmatic use (AlreadyExists checks, etc.).\n- Add errorHandler middleware (bff/src/middleware/errorHandler.ts) that\n  catches K8sApiError and returns only the HTTP status code and a generic\n  \"Kubernetes API request failed\" message — never the raw body.\n- Register the error handler in server.ts after all routes.\n- Add tests for the error handler covering K8sApiError sanitisation and\n  generic error fallback.\n- Extend k8sClient tests to assert that err.message excludes the body and\n  that err.body stores the raw response for server-side use.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings (round 1)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45eba05e5345b2b83608bed793747c33e5a7fa35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/45eba05e5345b2b83608bed793747c33e5a7fa35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/bdd0b623a42c055d422631aa71cc634fb811df23","verification":{"payload":"tree 45eba05e5345b2b83608bed793747c33e5a7fa35\nparent 4db700e96ea77f29e93988dc023f52f0eb11b8de\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784379633 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784379633 -0400\n\nfix(bff): sanitize K8sApiError body in Express error handler (#67)\n\n* fix(bff): sanitize K8sApiError body in Express error handler\n\n- Remove raw K8s response body from K8sApiError.message so it is never\n  accidentally forwarded to clients via err.message (e.g., in route-level\n  error arrays). The body is still available via err.body for server-side\n  programmatic use (AlreadyExists checks, etc.).\n- Add errorHandler middleware (bff/src/middleware/errorHandler.ts) that\n  catches K8sApiError and returns only the HTTP status code and a generic\n  \"Kubernetes API request failed\" message — never the raw body.\n- Register the error handler in server.ts after all routes.\n- Add tests for the error handler covering K8sApiError sanitisation and\n  generic error fallback.\n- Extend k8sClient tests to assert that err.message excludes the body and\n  that err.body stores the raw response for server-side use.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings (round 1)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW3jxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAah0QADg6590TVg+K6WxmBxDH6adI\nP1C5GhHAv7nxXCmgxkIMTimXJW7/ZI3DAmLjRyho+YQb+4WWxBwCFHesmJz6ClPI\nWp0YnlITEbl1b0NJtO6K0ipBZ0pKhE4h1kA+1jsb6tO5y6l1AJWBWPgWZ+pll8zQ\ngmZpTC0zOU8LRJn+KmU7I82yfep0AD9bWIGRDsvyYOlGC0ce7AQOMaeBV91y4Bmo\nJqz4ewCrSROkRUK71aH8Ghs1zd9zFKCNgN7PwQjNH0sIn9wctQ73XORhKRr51Wbq\n37OrzZFLDqeAkkH4w/9GQ3C2MaWwVNWWLV3adMiWIKgKABXERwIU/phdbOzq/p24\nfmEuDBJZgoOdYStSkRtn8apwXDI6sjJlxywvu8pVQP0EYHElg4ScSORRSi384vDu\n5/LgprhSCF/DjdUxgF00m9gwbiRiFaokbxTgNvOj6USOGqrya84BUT36Y8