"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/c0847ebf2cf114c475a6128e565a5cdc8b73cab9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:47:23Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:47:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(bff): extract shared httpRequest utility from k8sClient and supersetClient (#55)\n\nBoth clients duplicated the same HTTP plumbing: transport selection\n(http/https), chunk accumulation, JSON parsing, empty-body detection,\ntimeout handling, and error propagation.\n\nExtract that core into bff/src/utils/httpRequest.ts, parameterised on:\n- full URL (scheme/host/port/path/query)\n- method, headers, body, timeoutMs\n- TLS options (rejectUnauthorized, ca) applied only for HTTPS\n- makeError factory so each caller retains its own error type\n  (K8sApiError with body / SupersetApiError without)\n- lenientJson flag for Superset''s plain-text /health response\n\nk8sRequest and SupersetClient.request now delegate to httpRequest.\nAll class methods, loginPromise, doLogin, authenticatedRequest,\nSupersetApiError, and K8sApiError are preserved unchanged.\n\nAdd bff/__tests__/httpRequest.test.ts covering transport selection,\nURL construction, TLS options, body serialisation, JSON parsing\n(strict and lenient), timeout, and error events (21 new tests).\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb326ef5bd80810bae2005ef09c3771b90a3c5f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/eb326ef5bd80810bae2005ef09c3771b90a3c5f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/c0847ebf2cf114c475a6128e565a5cdc8b73cab9","verification":{"payload":"tree eb326ef5bd80810bae2005ef09c3771b90a3c5f7\nparent 9849734d4c012596345a1beb4c7e275b24347169\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784328443 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784328443 -0400\n\nchore(bff): extract shared httpRequest utility from k8sClient and supersetClient (#55)\n\nBoth clients duplicated the same HTTP plumbing: transport selection\n(http/https), chunk accumulation, JSON parsing, empty-body detection,\ntimeout handling, and error propagation.\n\nExtract that core into bff/src/utils/httpRequest.ts, parameterised on:\n- full URL (scheme/host/port/path/query)\n- method, headers, body, timeoutMs\n- TLS options (rejectUnauthorized, ca) applied only for HTTPS\n- makeError factory so each caller retains its own error type\n  (K8sApiError with body / SupersetApiError without)\n- lenientJson flag for Superset''s plain-text /health response\n\nk8sRequest and SupersetClient.request now delegate to httpRequest.\nAll class methods, loginPromise, doLogin, authenticatedRequest,\nSupersetApiError, and K8sApiError are preserved unchanged.\n\nAdd bff/__tests__/httpRequest.test.ts covering transport selection,\nURL construction, TLS options, body serialisation, JSON parsing\n(strict and lenient), timeout, and error events (21 new tests).\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWrD7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA35oQACR2LfLf0x/h32MlEUGql01K\nEpseZbLD5ZNaliGEXFuX/k7FCERuvvkE1kMyxVxVtlKU7TTqOZb3U8V7y183YX3v\nLF7930sZCbcy4e4ONO4PAwu+5zOutBWfxEAqx+lnGKMV8Z0QfzZDIhFVV8Np78Da\nhys6mbCG14ok490wAvs0KucQlgNapf/CF4Jynn4Js9fuOKnmIJMFIPQExbQe3j47\nFoJE3189xUgeTbWV3cJga4+Ndygg344ntt3NnxRhHnjdQpBwDYBrlI4XMTAP9bu7\nBqnuih36AZONrm+Rju3cEJFUq51bguw63cIyC/S9Tg0xb8tSb0GiGkCj5WeL7M7L\n0nXD52Vp7ir9yppIAv7PgpB+PbsXy81IqKiiPgiA711CdxXCGOIRLi85+eVyWjkw\n0DtnWNhNt/Pd63OkBWbFelR8TNUjzeUMvOqMvri/KEdr7lCh6d275Mw0Be1faCF2\nkCz8ZtOcA0hJ/DjEVkyRXPe5S4bLPhwKDVykj5a5bW2ZFIjyfD/Y/gdqMFBKaPgB\nX/ZzP7qZxp1Y+hEev3PT2G2jhAlMLyB6NO0pHUHShXPh+YfJ2AgDUwng95Ii8EUv\niOK6qXfZl2lgOWno3D732CQGIahnZdWZsopI2OFG5pkc1pTMU+jnnn89oGwp/PF2\n2zleedbTqeCZum51KZK0\n=Ps2h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T22:47:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/c0847ebf2cf114c475a6128e565a5cdc8b73cab9","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKGMwODQ3ZWJmMmNmMTE0YzQ3NWE2MTI4ZTU2NWE1Y2RjOGI3M2NhYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/9849734d4c012596345a1beb4c7e275b24347169","sha":"9849734d4c012596345a1beb4c7e275b24347169","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/9849734d4c012596345a1beb4c7e275b24347169"}],"sha":"c0847ebf2cf114c475a6128e565a5cdc8b73cab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/c0847ebf2cf114c475a6128e565a5cdc8b73cab9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/9849734d4c012596345a1beb4c7e275b24347169/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:35:49Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:35:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): fix undefined-as-T type safety in HTTP clients (#54)\n\nChange the return type of k8sRequest and SupersetClient.request from\nPromise<T> to Promise<T | undefined> to eliminate the unsafe\n`undefined as T` cast on empty (e.g. 204 No Content) responses.\n\nCallers that always expect a body (GET, POST, PUT) now throw a clear\nerror when the response is empty. DELETE callers that legitimately\nreceive no content accept undefined naturally via Promise<unknown>.\n\nAdds targeted tests for each undefined-guard path.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"795c961bc3c3e637ee730896bbbc35230d7c939f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/795c961bc3c3e637ee730896bbbc35230d7c939f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/9849734d4c012596345a1beb4c7e275b24347169","verification":{"payload":"tree 795c961bc3c3e637ee730896bbbc35230d7c939f\nparent cbea27ad9e5421fca62ac71f6e16eebc395c264d\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784327749 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784327749 -0400\n\nfix(bff): fix undefined-as-T type safety in HTTP clients (#54)\n\nChange the return type of k8sRequest and SupersetClient.request from\nPromise<T> to Promise<T | undefined> to eliminate the unsafe\n`undefined as T` cast on empty (e.g. 204 No Content) responses.\n\nCallers that always expect a body (GET, POST, PUT) now throw a clear\nerror when the response is empty. DELETE callers that legitimately\nreceive no content accept undefined naturally via Promise<unknown>.\n\nAdds targeted tests for each undefined-guard path.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWq5FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlUoQAAQu2OkBiTa9eIIjSEKyjap+\nVcnB5hAY83uxzgjsSb00ZBCNTQBDpXmuIgF4aJSbheFG3bom5TTTSEXA/WlXen1Q\nkA40LKu9lzz2HCj0P7NEwHu87bPwGgQXENmhiKSxIpB/Ol560QMUBYx3baM+eepK\nWK5G1PtP3njPFEsPCDuUU7bNTO/QpdSh1Z+5FcdY4lWucx4yz6+o6814JyPI9yFM\nFJyX6bXOjRcnckxMfdGE/rOKlpA68phe1C2zw5njJd3NYdkOHR5u7PGWcVIQ6g+M\nr88ohe5tKMfRDcog+ndUwublGYkKUf3TguEhxvgfyx/Dbz1tQi4nNUGv2Y6YNQ+L\n8wZ2b3Ax0/OrCG38nsevExctWYDRBkC6zH0p7Udh7eTeKxWKsMR5OUNuRt6pyAoW\nKHKFLpAhuS1j5FXmO4eiw3QgbpzTXQsbipEvfokk7P9NfjWsyT11mR+zjywymuic\ncVCUq9M6TMV/icHGIn9TpHr9s/9rI7TdhVgRltna7m5QcGQ21tXZMXcl4/GfqQc6\nVHoQn1RuiDEB3vQYKqXUDT9/lXEtEXl/cJ6lTb8PHpmxTWJSoTrfJxzIOboVaY3g\nyR9lLtcPYZLbdMI+Z/fPiZLALePEnhad8//+AU+gmJCBywvwRJfmn5biyxYOdoUG\ntfWmo09tFNOyMchf4OkQ\n=iXB4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"ve