imou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/cbea27ad9e5421fca62ac71f6e16eebc395c264d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:26:10Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:26:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): add pagination support to listDashboards (#53)\n\n- Accept optional page and pageSize parameters (default page=0, pageSize=100)\n- Return DashboardListResult with dashboards, totalCount, page, and pageSize\n- Update query URL to use provided parameters\n- Add DashboardListResult type to types.ts\n- Update existing tests and add new tests for explicit pagination params\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea976250d533ad69426ed6844be4c17fdb4a5563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/ea976250d533ad69426ed6844be4c17fdb4a5563"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/cbea27ad9e5421fca62ac71f6e16eebc395c264d","verification":{"payload":"tree ea976250d533ad69426ed6844be4c17fdb4a5563\nparent 6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784327170 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784327170 -0400\n\nfix(bff): add pagination support to listDashboards (#53)\n\n- Accept optional page and pageSize parameters (default page=0, pageSize=100)\n- Return DashboardListResult with dashboards, totalCount, page, and pageSize\n- Update query URL to use provided parameters\n- Add DashboardListResult type to types.ts\n- Update existing tests and add new tests for explicit pagination params\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWqwCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjKgQACTvd5itdRqxiMrRZIFp2AI+\n3HXPN/Rtrm+1refl8zalXCrxzFfAMLiJgVmTHVOGQ2gIHJO8KvzWa8N1/EjFRlZB\nvrw7nmbswoCmHdBO1BajzQfPmcc6rFGPADaJjoFbG/1urOo9A1jA7WIRAFp9XRg2\n1tk+7za8/jPedYu6XgqvORGzdHOufTLd+wjaTmc0XkQkf5taiE7o9XFI42/Mi77/\nCakJvFG7CfaqtgIlfRb+KkL2XellTLhrIP7WmPvXM9aQQkesbYpPTyzbAD/fcw10\nE2pQjg/xt8JzORBVKO1Xzr8xFLOod64U4ajfIXO6GotQfjavkyNMrbYvso5+haja\n+IXRNXG/GuQcK3ph5wyxWJkt0NTHv16erY7LtLvPCFrUKxmPTHYlFlWe1jbp+s1R\n4YclzEiSwRNvjDtC74bvFXOfMCfTgK5bLlVswUP6fvqPlOf1DJjaPeaTBjlACZYO\nU4vIdeJ9oWCGfaQK3hplgEy/h8pWPJYXYzf5XdJNsUAyYcPM6ZD50v2YoKXQykHf\nuvJpCIxxY17ToDPUhivbEFQxOyyc+B1CeG3tliCFnSWOHOCF0BjtBsOTZ9YXJr4/\nVC06zKxzKXBaY2cPtw3vXRj7hUKLuaGcxcgwt3pIBsAbu4f6RIljYvm5PSfbNZok\ny0ypjGRmI0uNV0TznlR8\n=JGhL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T22:26:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/cbea27ad9e5421fca62ac71f6e16eebc395c264d","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKGNiZWEyN2FkOWU1NDIxZmNhNjJhYzcxZjZlMTZlZWJjMzk1YzI2NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a","sha":"6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a"}],"sha":"cbea27ad9e5421fca62ac71f6e16eebc395c264d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/cbea27ad9e5421fca62ac71f6e16eebc395c264d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:26:08Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:26:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): implement scope rebinding for with blocks in helmRenderer (#52)\n\nIn real Helm, {{- with .Values.x }} rebinds `.` to the target object\ninside the block, so bare `.field` references resolve against the with\ntarget rather than the global values.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace `evaluateCondition` with `evaluateExpression` which returns\n  the resolved value (not just a boolean), enabling scope binding for\n  `with` blocks.\n- In `processConditionals`, when the keyword is `with` and the resolved\n  value is an object, call `applyWithScope` to substitute bare `.field`\n  and `.field | quote` references in the block body before the block is\n  removed.\n- Fix the body-matching regex to use a tempered greedy token\n  `((?:(?!\\{\\{-?\\s*(?:if|with)\\s)[\\s\\S])*?)` so the engine always\n  matches the truly innermost block first. This is required for nested\n  `with` blocks to resolve correctly (inner scope applied before outer).\n- Add `applyWithScope` helper that replaces `{{ .field }}` and\n  `{{ .field | quote }}` patterns against a given scope object, while\n  skipping fully-qualified `.Values.*`, `.Release.*`, `.Chart.*` refs.\n\nTests added:\n- Bare `.password` and `.host` references resolved against a `with` target\n- `.field | quote` pipe inside a `with` block\n- Nested `with` blocks, each rebound to its own scope\n- Falsy `with` target skips the block body\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a7f19fa9759462bd5c0aafafbdc2856e820e75e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/9a7f19fa9759462bd5c0aafafbdc2856e820e75e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a7f19fa9759462bd5c0aafafbdc2856e820e75e\nparent b8edfc24a357e6438c3101ff7fb42f8aae57dfc1\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784327168 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784327168 -0400\n\nfix(bff): implement scope rebinding for with blocks in helmRenderer (#52)\n\nIn real Helm, {{- with .Values.x }} rebinds `.` to the target object\ninside the block, so bare `.field` references resolve against the with\ntarget rather than the global values.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace `evaluateCondition` with `evaluateExpression` which returns\n  the resolved value (not just a boolean), enabling scope binding for\n  `with` blocks.\n- In `processConditionals`, when the keyword is `with` and the resolved\n  value is an object, call `applyWithScope` to substitute bare `.field`\n  and `.field | quote` references in the block body before the block is\n  removed.\n- Fix the body-matching regex to use a tempered greedy token\n  `((?:(?!\\{\\{-?\\s*(?:if|with)\\s)[\\s\\S])*?)` so the engine always\n  matches the truly innermost block first. This is required for nested\n  `with` blocks to resolve correctly (inner scope applied before outer).\n- Add `applyWithScope` helper that replaces `{{ .field }}` and\n  `{{ .field | quote }}` patterns against a given scope object, while\n  skipping fully-qualified `.Values.*`, `.Release.*`, `.Chart.*` refs.\n\nTests added:\n- Bare `.password` and `.host` references resolved against a `with` target\n- `.field | quote` pipe inside a `with` block\n- Nested `with` blocks, each rebound to its own scope\n- Falsy `with` target skips the block body\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWqwACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZa0QAD05rghR5SkK1VZBY1e7HDba\nfrnBwZXiPJduGFzXQdCnXUz8U4d1NQAcmqDHJMBlfg/9foLzz2nXsltDo4NkAYVW\nWnVsB4SyTpuqtJb+drejCj6eMffP9DDcThcNS2gK+uOOSR/o0SmkoY37Z1qF4nS4\nP6yWNj2bMzyb02CC887i/GZU4YKOpYrm+HsfZ91YSRd13GvCRV3Jte2saSlCqgjW\nCWEW8V2XNbHg9eAOMDX2ZZjwNMQPca2HKlkcf1ANAEAMOgmaXVKWP7nXydf1MhdX\n5JdlOZYM8b37GpE3P3y1UL9+7n3dIka01pLRHQQKQ3kQeNAJ/gWVoW6TAfvfKx88\ndEXMQw2NGezZcstFDfFDQVRWIOq6VqdQiiHZpAKpPwMZCezG5bKsZ+Xlc6SaatG7\nOLc6LHgjKjV2Ctf4ZR+aUnnOklA2O31yfpRJrf1wOeJntVIrknWEQto/s+nhXsgC\n7PB82P7gMv/VF5g6RnXCm+QikVi/N0JxvspHC4DlgTSXqTUv/hT/B0XNO2UIWJqH\nz/aDk3/hJm/RgDMSoK+cTlZWR0o1T/Ag/ZgZh3sRG5H7PxGzKmlH0LMYxUT4wkG2\n9JCIMWCbild2md98s/7wszaflY6E6bz3TtQKq3I2KGhkeIImmsgSSrMADi+0AW6Z\nQttOXeP1c/AW9mvOKsSl\n=td63\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T22:26:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a","node_id":"C_kwDOTbpVO9oAKDY1NTVkMDM5MWY4ZjYxZjJhNDNmZWY2YzFhYTU5MDE2ZGI2M2E5MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commit/b8edfc24a357e6438c3101ff7fb42f8aae57dfc1","sha":"b8edfc24a357e6438c3101ff7fb42f8aae57dfc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/b8edfc24a357e6438c3101ff7fb42f8aae57dfc1"}],"sha":"6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/6555d0391f8f61f2a43fef6c1aa59016db63a90a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/commits/b8edfc24a357e6438c3101ff7fb42f8aae57dfc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:09:26Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T22:09:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): invalidate cached token and retry on 401 in SupersetClient (#51)\n\n* fix(bff): invalidate cached token and retry on 401 in SupersetClient\n\nOn a 401 response from an authenticated request, clear cachedAccessToken\nand loginPromise then retry once with a freshly obtained token. If the\nretry also returns 401 the error is propagated to the caller. Introduce\nSupersetApiError (carrying statusCode) so the retry logic can reliably\ndistinguish 401s from other HTTP errors. Add tests covering the retry\nsuccess path, the double-401 propagation path, and the error class itself.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings on 401-retry change\n\n- Rewrite authenticatedRequest JSDoc to explain WHY retry is needed\n  (server-side JWT revocation before client TTL expiry) rather than\n  describing the mechanics\n- Add test: non-401 errors (500) are propagated immediately without retry\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86f9027d8c03cd53370ded4ae36a69843c64d3b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/trees/86f9027d8c03cd53370ded4ae36a69843c64d3b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/apache-superset/git/commits/b8edfc24a357e6438c3101ff7fb42f8aae57dfc1","verification":{"payload":"tree 86f9027d8c03cd53370ded4ae36a69843c64d3b2\nparent 9086b99fd9727af59141cd4419f6c417810d7c62\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784326166 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784326166 -0400\n\nfix(bff): invalidate cached token and retry on 401 in SupersetClient (#51)\n\n* fix(bff): invalidate cached token and retry on 401 in SupersetClient\n\nOn a 401 response from an authenticated request, clear cachedAccessToken\nand loginPromise then retry once with a freshly obtained token. If the\nretry also returns 401 the error is propagated to the caller. Introduce\nSupersetApiError (carrying statusCode) so the retry logic can reliably\ndistinguish 401s from other HTTP errors. Add tests covering the retry\nsuccess path, the double-401 propagation path, and the error class itself.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): address review findings on 401-retry change\n\n- Rewrite authenticatedRequest JSDoc to explain WHY retry is needed\n  (server-side JWT revocation before client TTL expiry) rather than\n  describing the mechanics\n- Add test: non-401 errors (500) are propagated immediately without retry\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWqgWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqTkQAIE4TXqvcSpWUmOJfvCL/kbo\n1I/KlLWdAvG+5DDIFkxjmzCqMGKqErcDP+na94gIOR0nxC/Vk/J3oPx5ZNqGYYKu\nCtJQetdQIa7XIgnki5Q2E/ATqc0mjFL98NuagQRzErUHSG7FLjeKurEQzqQpasgR\njy2WDV5YEkAzCrsLnV+hGXLTZnFPXm7Y/GLADD7mUTgX0pazbZPo36pSWJxwm5q3\nq8dPnCxUVNXMmyF8KKumWV7Z6H/Z8Kh83DF/FuHAbAbE1TzT+7GBXZdBZlXVcvMO\n5vN+ccbkMY51OALuKfoWfZCaEKLJAdICs3kDQkW8JcSg6QnNR+rT1uwZqScGAirX\npWb/RBPwP/AjoMWabcbwAPGkSJZ7Rv+0iE4QO+EFl0RT4XEW0WLoGBbJCvY8XCpf\nRHB3XwRss+Mwj++x963BI/Y0P+l1cMbBy76Cf25x7IlcMNvJD2Egizowrx+x+HJZ\nBK72v2ueX3WQF1ObcrP+J2tGrs+kOAMIWMhuZDEKJLHKs5CNOoEPZbJhyEy4LWnX\nkge2hyLf1kP3XjGqCbkcP4AdpWiL1q//0BYqBn6vpF2Oc4iIWG/NOgFveGiry5Xo\n2oR3kvEDtI9Hno/ARQHhROLTQzWtk9Kd2NiW5EZ52Mpv3OwgPSJuYTtGUJZR754F\n76AekC0grPbHuR/MpBqr\n=344c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T22:09:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","fol