repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/857b23c739efb403e0e73fbd932966db8178dec6","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDg1N2IyM2M3MzllZmI0MDNlMGU3M2ZiZDkzMjk2NmRiODE3OGRlYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/471a58c909d745e924ee7790121cb9c2f91aa570","sha":"471a58c909d745e924ee7790121cb9c2f91aa570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/471a58c909d745e924ee7790121cb9c2f91aa570"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/c1064a5ff017a8a717d602bf6787d030da34e807","sha":"c1064a5ff017a8a717d602bf6787d030da34e807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/c1064a5ff017a8a717d602bf6787d030da34e807"}],"sha":"857b23c739efb403e0e73fbd932966db8178dec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/857b23c739efb403e0e73fbd932966db8178dec6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/c1064a5ff017a8a717d602bf6787d030da34e807/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:26:59Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:05:33Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: pets, cs2-lib 9.5.0, cs2-lib-inspect\n\ncs2-lib 9.5.0 adds pets (the round-start chicken: egg, chick, and three\nbreeds), and the CS2 plugin reads them from a new `pet` key on the equipped\nv5 feed (ianlucas/cs2-css-inventory-simulator#150).\n\nPets\n- New `pet` loadout slot, shared across teams, sitting beside Pin / Medal:\n  the extras grid now pairs [Pin / Medal | Pet] on the last row instead of\n  Pin / Medal spanning it.\n- owned_items gains `style` and `upgrade_level` (null = the pet''s default).\n  Validated with cs2-lib''s own validators; the egg takes no name tag and\n  only breeds have styles / a stage choice.\n- v5 feed `pet` entry mirrors upstream field for field: def, nametag,\n  petId, seed, style (omitted when stock), uid, upgradeLevel (always sent,\n  so an egg stays an egg).\n- Craft editor: Style and Stage selects plus a plain Pattern input; share\n  links carry style/stage. Armory gets a Pets section, ItemSpecs shows a\n  pet''s style and stage.\n- Flat econ icon only — 3D is deferred (TODO.md). Icons come through the\n  existing manifest on the next extraction run.\n\nInspect links\n- Replace the hand-rolled protobuf writer with @ianlucas/cs2-lib-inspect.\n  Rows are repaired onto cs2-lib''s grid first; sticker rotation keeps our\n  0.1 degree precision so the link and the server feed still agree.\n- Over-length links come back as a console command, which the UI now\n  copies to the clipboard instead of navigating to.\n- tools/inspect-roundtrip.ts ported to the new entry point, with pet\n  coverage (petindex, style, upgrade_level, variation pattern).","tree":{"sha":"7a85b149abfc0530575eccd58d94145e6e7c767f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/7a85b149abfc0530575eccd58d94145e6e7c767f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/c1064a5ff017a8a717d602bf6787d030da34e807","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a85b149abfc0530575eccd58d94145e6e7c767f\nparent 471a58c909d745e924ee7790121cb9c2f91aa570\nauthor Luke Policinski <luke@lukepolo.com> 1791055619 +0000\ncommitter Luke Policinski <luke@lukepolo.com> 1791065133 +0000\n\nfeature: pets, cs2-lib 9.5.0, cs2-lib-inspect\n\ncs2-lib 9.5.0 adds pets (the round-start chicken: egg, chick, and three\nbreeds), and the CS2 plugin reads them from a new `pet` key on the equipped\nv5 feed (ianlucas/cs2-css-inventory-simulator#150).\n\nPets\n- New `pet` loadout slot, shared across teams, sitting beside Pin / Medal:\n  the extras grid now pairs [Pin / Medal | Pet] on the last row instead of\n  Pin / Medal spanning it.\n- owned_items gains `style` and `upgrade_level` (null = the pet''s default).\n  Validated with cs2-lib''s own validators; the egg takes no name tag and\n  only breeds have styles / a stage choice.\n- v5 feed `pet` entry mirrors upstream field for field: def, nametag,\n  petId, seed, style (omitted when stock), uid, upgradeLevel (always sent,\n  so an egg stays an egg).\n- Craft editor: Style and Stage selects plus a plain Pattern input; share\n  links carry style/stage. Armory gets a Pets section, ItemSpecs shows a\n  pet''s style and stage.\n- Flat econ icon only — 3D is deferred (TODO.md). Icons come through the\n  existing manifest on the next extraction run.\n\nInspect links\n- Replace the hand-rolled protobuf writer with @ianlucas/cs2-lib-inspect.\n  Rows are repaired onto cs2-lib''s grid first; sticker rotation keeps our\n  0.1 degree precision so the link and the server feed still agree.\n- Over-length links come back as a console command, which the UI now\n  copies to the clipboard instead of navigating to.\n- tools/inspect-roundtrip.ts ported to the new entry point, with pet\n  coverage (petindex, style, upgrade_level, variation pattern).\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIQKxfRw\nz1iOm9wqXHmp+BRZXfBtakatdxhEUgJJFKFK3xEJGoeGHsEz37O/fbZrn8Odl+nCQXhm03P0HZ5F\nswQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/c1064a5ff017a8a717d602bf6787d030da34e807","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKGMxMDY0YTVmZjAxN2E4YTcxN2Q2MDJiZjY3ODdkMDMwZGEzNGU4MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/471a58c909d745e924ee7790121cb9c2f91aa570","sha":"471a58c909d745e924ee7790121cb9c2f91aa570","url":"https://api.github.com/