"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/68cce30c6e5a06de19231b5edf5d2949ab41fa92"}],"sha":"4f9ec6e8074bb5b2b5547f7cc7b64817a99f6f3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/4f9ec6e8074bb5b2b5547f7cc7b64817a99f6f3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/68cce30c6e5a06de19231b5edf5d2949ab41fa92/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:28:46Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:28:46Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"merge: eleven inventory features onto the pricing branch\n\nBrings in integration/inventory-wave1: public loadout attachments, collections\nbrowser, inspect animation, loadout presets, StatTrak history, recently-added\nsort, favourites + wishlist, lighting presets, compare, save-image, and the\ni18n/sort-mode guardrails.\n\nmain.ts, viewer3d.ts, catalog.ts, routes.ts, devFlags.ts and style.css all\nauto-merged. Five files conflicted, every one of them because both sides\nAPPENDED to the same registry rather than because they disagreed:\n\n  schema.sql     prices/price_history vs stattrak_kills/wishlist — union\n  api.ts         PricePoint fields vs public-loadout attachments — union\n  ItemTile.vue   the icon import: your side dropped Link2/RefreshCw with their\n                 usages, mine added Heart. Resolved to what the merged template\n                 actually renders, which is neither side''s list.\n  sortModes.ts   \"value\" vs \"recent\"/\"collection\". Hand-merged: a union would\n                 have left two \"];\" and an array entry outside the array.\n  App.vue        six hunks. Two needed hand-merging because both sides ended\n                 mid-expression sharing one closing tail — a union would have\n                 left the value comparator unterminated.\n\nTwo things the merge would have silently lost, and did not:\n\n  - The StatTrak kill-history panel. Your side extracted the read-only spec into\n    ItemSpecs.vue, which renders the counter but not the record behind it; the\n    127-line history block lived in the markup that extraction replaced. Ported\n    into ItemSpecs with killHistory as a prop, for the same reason charmAlbedo is\n    one: the component is handed an item, the fetch belongs to whoever knows the\n    modal is open. The focus stage deliberately does NOT get it — the watch that\n    loads the ledger is gated on view mode, so focus would render an empty box.\n  - Value sorting on catalog lists. needsOwnedItem covers wear and recent; value\n    keeps its own gate, because that one turns on whether the operator has a feed\n    rather than on what kind of list it is.\n\nAlso fixes tools/schema-lint.mjs, which this merge tripped. It scans for\nCREATE TABLE ... \\n); with a regex and does not exclude prose, so a COMMENT\ncontaining the words \"CREATE TABLE\" — one does, in the presets section — started\na match inside the comment, ran to the next \");\" a hundred lines later, swallowed\na dollar-quoted DO block and reported every PL/pgSQL keyword in it as a\nreserved-word column. Nine confident failures pointing at nothing. It now strips\nline comments first, and still catches a real reserved-word column.\n\nYour check:sfc caught something vue-tsc passed: I had put an HTML comment inside\na tag''s attribute list. Fixed.\n\nVerified on the merged tree: npm run check (typecheck, slots, inspect, stattrak,\nsteam-sync, prices, sfc, schema) all green, plus i18n-check and sort-modes-check.","tree":{"sha":"bcf5980a4ef1125fce4db9214bf4c1f828bf1814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/bcf5980a4ef1125fce4db9214bf4c1f828bf1814"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/68cce30c6e5a06de19231b5edf5d2949ab41fa92","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/68cce30c6