/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/7d2d598cdb80a155ed0521c36223ff61833b00cd","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDdkMmQ1OThjZGI4MGExNTVlZDA1MjFjMzYyMjNmZjYxODMzYjAwY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","sha":"126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f"}],"sha":"7d2d598cdb80a155ed0521c36223ff61833b00cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/7d2d598cdb80a155ed0521c36223ff61833b00cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/9ad01473469e7940edfdb73d3afc8cf83c219988/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:41:39Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:41:39Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"tools: check translation keys against the catalogue, and fix the two it found\n\ntr(key, fallback) is total: a key the catalogue does not have renders the English\nfallback, forever. That is the right runtime behaviour — a missing translation\nmust never blank a button — but it makes every mistake here invisible from the\nscreen. Three failure shapes, none of which show up in review:\n\n  1. Used and not in the catalogue. The UI looks perfect and the string is\n     unreachable to a translator, so the day a second locale exists that control\n     is silently still English. Armory had two of these.\n  2. In the catalogue and never used. Dead weight, and worse than dead: someone\n     pays to translate a string nobody will ever see.\n  3. THE DRIFT — catalogue text and in-code fallback have diverged. English users\n     get one wording, every reader of the code sees the other, and neither is\n     wrong enough to notice until someone \"fixes\" the code to match the screen.\n\n(3) cannot be found by reading either file alone, which is why this compares TEXT\nand not just key presence.\n\nFixed: inventory.armory.search and inventory.armory.drill were called and absent.\nAdded with the exact fallback text, because a paraphrase would have traded one\nfailure for the subtler one.\n\nTwo things I got wrong while writing it, both now the point of the comments:\n\n  - The first matcher used [^''\"] for the fallback, which excludes the quote that\n    did NOT open the string — so any fallback containing an apostrophe never\n    matched. It reported 36 unused keys that were all in use. A tool that is\n    blind exactly where English is punctuated is worse than no tool.\n  - Several fallbacks are template literals, because they interpolate a count or\n    an error. Those are USED but not text-comparable, so drift checking skips\n    them and the summary says how many rather than implying they were checked.\n\nThe unused list is a WARNING and stays one. AdminConsole builds its extraction\nlabels as tr(`...steps.${s.name}`), so ten live keys look dead to any static\nreader; the tool counts computed-key calls and says so rather than pretending.\nFailing on that would train people to ignore it.\n\nNegative-tested both failing arms: a drifted value and a deleted key each produce\nexactly one correct failure.","tree":{"sha":"9cb65a090e0fa7ed8248a5463cb446d808acfdde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/9cb65a090e0fa7ed8248a5463cb446d808acfdde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/9ad01473469e7940edfdb73d3afc8cf83c219988","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/9ad01473469e7940edfdb73d3afc8cf83c219988","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDlhZDAxNDczNDY5ZTc5NDBlZGZkYjczZDNhZmM4Y2Y4M2MyMTk5ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56","sha":"fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56"}],"sha":"9ad01473469e7940edfdb73d3afc8cf83c219988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/9ad01473469e7940edfdb73d3afc8cf83c219988"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:30:12Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:30:12Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: save the 3D stage as a PNG\n\nThe renderer could already do this. snapshot() is how every item card is baked,\nand it had exactly one caller — the bake queue — so the picture this app is best\nat making was the one thing you could not take away from it. routes.ts opens by\nexplaining that a screenshot cannot carry the state a link can; this is the other\nhalf of that argument, and the half that was missing.\n\nCaptures the LIVE stage rather than re-mounting an offscreen one, so you get the\nangle you framed instead of a canonical three-quarter view. That is the point: if\nthe interesting thing about a pattern is only visible from one side, a standard\npose does not capture it.\n\nOn the focus stage and on compare. A null blob is the viewer''s way of saying\n\"nothing to capture\" (a model that never finished, a lost context), so that path\nnotifies rather than failing silently — a button that does nothing reads as a\nbroken click. The object URL is revoked on a timer rather than immediately,\nbecause some browsers have not started reading the blob when click() returns and\nrevoking first cancels the save.\n\nVerified: typecheck and all five verifiers. NOT verified: the download itself.\nThere is no browser here, so the anchor-click save path has never run.","tree":{"sha":"7d1f7954dfb95f7e2fcdd5fc21de663b8c618e7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/7d1f7954dfb95f7e2fcdd5fc21de663b8c618e7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKGZkODEyNzk0Zjg2MzQ3NmYxZjE3N2ExZDNjOGUzZDhkYjVjMjllNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50","sha":"a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50"}],"sha":"fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/fd812794f863476f1f177a1d3c8e3d8db5c29e56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:20:30Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:20:30Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: compare two owned items on one stage, under one camera\n\nA/B blink, not two panes side by side, for two reasons and the second is the\nbetter one.\n\nThere is exactly ONE live WebGL viewer at a time. That rule is enforced\neverywhere here because a second live context is the orphan that renders a gun\nbelow the pane, and useViewerMount exists specifically to guarantee it. Two panes\nwould mean breaking it.\n\nBut blink is also the better instrument. Two images an inch apart are compared by\neye across a gap; two images in the SAME pixels a second apart are compared by\nchange, and the eye is far better at spotting change than difference. It is the\nsame reason PatternScoreRail already blinks a pinned pattern against the live one\nrather than showing them side by side.\n\nBlink only works if the camera does not move between the two, which is what the\nnew ViewerOpts.camera and ViewerHandle.cameraState are for: the pose is read off\nthe outgoing mount and handed to the incoming one, so the item swaps underneath a\ncamera that stays put. The override is applied AFTER framing, so everything\nframing derives — the pivot, the frustum height, the upright chest-lift — is\nstill computed, and only the eye and pivot are then replaced. Guarded on all six\nnumbers being finite, because a half-populated pose puts the eye at NaN and three\nrenders that as nothing rather than as an error.\n\nIt is a ROUTE, /compare/:a/:b, not just an overlay. This plugin''s stated rule is\nthat every screen and modal is a URL, and the reason given in routes.ts applies\nhere exactly: a comparison is the most shareable thing in the app and useless to\ndescribe in prose. Both ids are in the PATH rather than the query because a\ncomparison is not a filter on a screen, it IS the screen, and it is meaningless\nwith one of them missing — which is also why comparePair resolves to null unless\nBOTH items are found rather than mounting the one that resolved.\n\nThe payload builder is deliberately NOT shared with the focus stage. Focus has to\ncope with a loadout DEFAULT that has no instance behind it, so every field there\nfalls back through the row; compare is only ever handed owned items, so those\nfallbacks would be dead branches pretending to be live ones.\n\nEntry is the existing bulk select, at exactly two — a Compare button that greys\nout at one or three explains itself less well than one that appears when the\nthing it does becomes possible.\n\nVerified: typecheck, all five verifiers, and a route table regression covering\nevery existing path plus the new one round-tripping. NOT verified: anything\nvisual. No CS2 assets and no browser here, so the mount payload and the camera\ncarry-over have never been seen to run.","tree":{"sha":"8f4ccc61bd6d31ca47c1344ec4412645f600d99f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/8f4ccc61bd6d31ca47c1344ec4412645f600d99f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKGE2MTQxMDE1OTNmYWIzMTMzMTQxOTI0ZTM1ZGJhODg5ZDVmZmNhNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1","sha":"232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1"}],"sha":"a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/a614101593fab3133141924e35dba889d5ffca50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:09:10Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:09:10Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: lighting presets for the 3D viewer\n\nFour rigs — Studio, Showcase, Warm, Dark — because a skin does not look like one\nthing, and which lighting is \"right\" is the argument the community actually has.\n\nThis is far smaller than it looks because ViewerOpts.lighting already existed as\na tools/shadertest calibration hook that production never passed. Every number\ngoes through that same seam: no light is added, moved, renamed or restructured,\nwhich matters because the inspect-motion code rotates the rig as a group at\nrender time and references those lights by name.\n\nStudio IS the calibrated default, value for value, so the default preset is a\ngenuine no-op. It is spelled out rather than left as an absent override so\n\"which rig am I looking at\" has an answer on every preset, and so a re-tune\nchanges one table instead of hunting scattered fallback literals.\n\nCARD BAKES IGNORE THE SETTING and pin to Studio. A baked card is cached forever\nagainst its render key, so a preset baked into one is indistinguishable from a\nbug — the same argument that already forces bloom off for bakes. Precedence is\nopts.lighting (shadertest) > Studio when still > the user''s pick.\n\ndevFlags gains a third kind of setting. A flag answers \"which code path\" and a\nnumber answers \"how much\"; this answers \"which one\". Encoding four rigs as three\nbooleans would make half the combinations meaningless. Stored values are\nvalidated against the declared options, so a key from a build that offered a\npreset this one dropped falls back to Studio rather than reaching the renderer.\n\nA test caught a real bug before commit: setFlag and resetFlags end with the same\ntwo lines, so a first-match replace put the choice-clearing loop in setFlag —\ntoggling bloom would have silently wiped your lighting rig, and Reset would not\nhave cleared it. Moved, and both directions are now asserted.\n\nAlso corrects a stale conclusion in BUTANE-BUDDY.md, which said bloom \"is the\nnext thing to build\" while a later section of the same document said bloom is on\nby default. Bloom shipped; the bubble claim is now a testable prediction, and the\nDark rig is the sharper tool for testing it. Nobody has looked yet, and the note\nnow says so.","tree":{"sha":"391460c654171274cbd5322287985d5834946564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/391460c654171274cbd5322287985d5834946564"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDIzMmJhNTNmZjA4N2I3ZjJhY2NkNjdmMTgzNGQ2NWM1ZDdjYTU1YjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7","sha":"bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7"}],"sha":"232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/232ba53ff087b7f2accd67f1834d65c5d7ca55b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:50:41Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:50:41Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: favourites for owned items, and a wishlist for ones you don''t\n\nTwo shapes, because favourite means two things and only one is a row you own.\nAn owned instance gets a boolean column — one fact about an existing row, where\na side table would add a join to every inventory read. A CATALOG item cannot: it\nis not in owned_items and will not be until someone crafts it, so the wishlist\nis its own table keyed by cs2-lib item id.\n\nThe owned flag is deliberately NOT gated on origin. The update route refuses\norigin=''steam'' rows because editing an imported item would make the mirror lie\nabout a real Steam inventory, but a favourite says nothing about the item, only\nabout the person looking at it — and refusing to star imports would make the\nfeature useless for the people with the most items.\n\nBoth routes take the desired STATE, not a toggle: a double-click on a toggle\nfires twice and lands back where it started, and the client already knows which\nway the heart points. Wishlist inserts are ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING so starring\ntwice is neither an error nor a reordering.\n\nThe heart is a <span role=button>, NOT a <button>. The tile root is itself a\nbutton and a nested one is invalid HTML that browsers silently reparent, which\ndrops the handler — the heart would have rendered and done nothing. TileActions\nalready documents this; I wrote the bug first and then read the comment.\n\nThe filter hides itself until something is starred, rather than disabling:\n''favourites only'' over an inventory with none is a control whose only outcome is\nan empty grid. It is also absent from STICKY_QUERY_KEYS — ''the ones I starred''\nis not a view of an inventory anyone else can open.\n\nVerified against a throwaway postgres:16: schema applied three times with no\nerrors, pre-existing rows survived and defaulted to false (not null), the index\nis genuinely partial, double-star is a no-op that does not move created_at, and\nthe planner does choose the partial index for the real query.","tree":{"sha":"796422667e4794d7cb0a49f38c18913a6921cb28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/796422667e4794d7cb0a49f38c18913a6921cb28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKGJkYmRiMTFjMDYwN2Q1NzNlOTc4MjVjMmQzZDM1NzU1ZTJkNzk2Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/58e1800bf8c05df74d9d3d2a077232070ac2affb","sha":"58e1800bf8c05df74d9d3d2a077232070ac2affb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/58e1800bf8c05df74d9d3d2a077232070ac2affb"}],"sha":"bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/bdbdb11c0607d573e97825c2d3d35755e2d796c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/58e1800bf8c05df74d9d3d2a077232070ac2affb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T16:52:19Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T16:52:19Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: sort an inventory by when things arrived\n\nAdds the ''Recently added'' item sort. owned_items.created_at has existed since\nthe first migration and nothing ever read it — the inventory offered default,\nrarity, name and wear, so ''what did I just craft'' was only answerable by\nscrolling.\n\nThe comparator breaks ties on the id, because a craft loop mints several rows\ninside one clock tick and a comparator returning 0 on genuinely different items\nlets their order flicker between renders. An undated row sorts to the old end in\neither direction, which is also how an older backend that never sends the field\ndegrades.\n\nAlso replaces the two hand-spelled ''is this wear on a catalog list'' conditions\nwith one needsOwnedItem predicate. wear needed a float and recent needs a date;\na catalog entry has neither, and the condition was already duplicated twice\nbefore this added a third case. SORTS_WITHOUT_WEAR is deliberately untouched: it\nis dead (no call sites anywhere) and the pricing branch is actively editing it.\n\ntools/sort-modes-check.ts closes the one hole tsc cannot see. SORT_NATURAL,\nSORT_DIR_HINT and SORT_DIR_KIND are Record<SortMode, ...> so a missing key fails\nto compile, but SORTS is an ARRAY: a mode can exist, sort correctly, and simply\nnever be offered, and the grid then looks merely unchanged. Negative-tested both\narms.","tree":{"sha":"6ed9431e479019c4d8e0e98aee040f1f8441595c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/6ed9431e479019c4d8e0e98aee040f1f8441595c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/58e1800bf8c05df74d9d3d2a077232070ac2affb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com