:"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/e00e88c3f6f5dc2f53ff4cbbf684bda6c36955e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/57afaa635e3dcafeeb704bbfe708d967f8cf45a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/57afaa635e3dcafeeb704bbfe708d967f8cf45a2","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDU3YWZhYTYzNWUzZGNhZmVlYjcwNGJiZmU3MDhkOTY3ZjhjZjQ1YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/524d156a3225eee4f40f759b861ed31cb7899cff","sha":"524d156a3225eee4f40f759b861ed31cb7899cff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/524d156a3225eee4f40f759b861ed31cb7899cff"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7","sha":"d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7"}],"sha":"57afaa635e3dcafeeb704bbfe708d967f8cf45a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/57afaa635e3dcafeeb704bbfe708d967f8cf45a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/4db019537eeeab0a4630d1ee63a3eb338626b1df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T16:01:23Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T16:01:23Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: loadout presets — named builds, one-click switching\n\nCS2 ships five loadout slots; ours allowed exactly one, and because the\nloadout is craft-gated against owned instances, rebuilding a rack of 15\nslots by hand is more work here than in the game.\n\nThe shape is deliberately lopsided. The preset you are WEARING has no rows\nof its own — its slots ARE inventory.loadout, unchanged — and only the\npresets you are not wearing park their slots in the new\ninventory.loadout_preset_slots. Activating swaps the two sets over inside a\ntransaction. The alternative (a preset_id folded into inventory.loadout''s\nprimary key) was rejected because /api/equipped/v5 is the hottest read in\nthe system: every game server hits it, unauthenticated, for every player on\nevery connect. A preset_id in that key would make it carry a \"which preset\nis active\" lookup forever, and would put a preset filter into five other\nloadout queries besides. As it stands, not one existing query changed.\n\nMigration moves ZERO rows: every player with a loadout today gets a preset\nnamed \"Loadout 1\" marked active, and their existing rows stay exactly where\nthey are. There is no step that writes to inventory.loadout, so there is no\nstep that can lose a build. main.ts mints the same row lazily for players\nwho have never equipped anything.\n\nDuplicating a preset does NOT clone owned items the way copy-from/:steamId\ndoes — both presets point at the same instances, because crafting is the\ngate and a preset is only an arrangement of what you already own.\n\nON DELETE CASCADE is kept on the new table''s item_instance_id, so deleting\nan owned item now empties that slot in every preset. That is the decision:\nthe loadout is craft-gated, so a slot whose instance is gone has nothing\nlegal left to hold, and RESTRICT would fail an inventory delete because of a\npreset the player is not looking at. The confirmation copy that now\nunderstates this is logged in TODO.md.\n\nTHE SLOT WHITELIST: presets doubled the number of tables storing a `slot`,\nso schema.sql''s boot-time cleanup now writes the list ONCE into a legal_slot\nCTE and deletes from both tables through it — two literal copies would have\nbeen the graffiti trap again, one table deeper. SLOT_RE and that list were\nre-read side by side and assert equal (23 slots).\n\nVerified against a throwaway Postgres: schema.sql applied three times over a\nseeded pre-feature database (loadouts intact, one active preset each, no\nduplicate presets), then the routes exercised end to end — duplicate,\nactivate, diverge, switch back (the parked build round-trips intact), the\nv5 feed following the switch, rename, the five-preset cap, deleting the\nbuild you are wearing, the last-preset refusal, the cross-account 404s, and\nthe cascade crossing into a parked preset.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6788969bf0c22d80e32fa9103e4182d3d9990f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/e6788969bf0c22d80e32fa9103e4182d3d9990f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/4db019537eeeab0a4630d1ee63a3eb338626b1df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/4db019537eeeab0a4630d1ee63a3eb338626b1df","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDRkYjAxOTUzN2VlZWFiMGE0NjMwZDFlZTYzYTNlYjMzODYyNmIxZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","sha":"126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f"}],"sha":"4db019537eeeab0a4630d1ee63a3eb338626b1df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/4db019537eeeab0a4630d1ee63a3eb338626b1df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/ccca987de78b7057700615119f438ec6f06813c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:58:36Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:58:36Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: StatTrak history — a kill ledger with real match context\n\nThe counter incremented and stored nothing else. It now leaves a record.\n\ninventory.stattrak_kills is append-only: one row per counted kill, with the\nitem instance, when, and whatever match context resolved at write time. The\ngame plugin''s payload carries no match id, so the only cheap moment to answer\n\"which match?\" is while it is still Live and the player is still in its\nlineup — killLedger.ts joins public.matches / match_lineup_players /\nmatch_maps / maps, driven from the live matches rather than from the player,\nand caches the answer per player for 30s. What it stores is a snapshot, not a\nforeign key: those tables belong to the panel, and a deployment pointed at a\nbare Postgres has none of them. The first 42P01 turns the join off for the\nlife of the process and kills keep logging with a null match.\n\nA failed ledger insert cannot cost the counter. The UPDATE is its own\ncommitted statement and the insert happens after it, outside any transaction,\nin a function that does not throw. Wrapping the pair would let a full disk\nroll back a kill a player has already watched tick over — and the endpoint is\nfire-and-forget from the game server, so nothing would ever retry it. The\ninsert is awaited rather than fired and forgotten, purely for backpressure.\n\nowned_items.stattrak_count stays the source of truth for the number, and stays\nout of the card render key. count(*) in the ledger is normally lower than it —\nkills counted before the ledger existed have no row and never will — so the\nitem view says \"N of M\" instead of pretending to be complete.\n\nThe item detail surface grows a history block in the read-only spec column:\nthe count, a 30-day trend, first kill, best map, matches, and the last three\nlegs. The loadout header gets the rack rollup, summed off the counters the\nloadout rows already carry rather than out of the ledger, so it needs no\nrequest and counts the pre-ledger kills too.\n\nKill history is more revealing than a loadout, so it is owner-only:\nGET /api/inventory/:id/kills is scoped to the caller and has no public\ncounterpart. /api/loadout/:steamId and the equipped feed are untouched and\nstill carry no kill data.\n\nOne index, (item_instance_id, killed_at) — the only read path, and the one the\nON DELETE CASCADE needs. Growth and the partitioning question are measured\nrather than assumed; see TODO.md, along with the live check the match join\nstill needs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6734193444feee5247fd7558eb72b6c3e0213634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/6734193444feee5247fd7558eb72b6c3e0213634"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/ccca987de78b7057700615119f438ec6f06813c8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/ccca987de78b7057700615119f438ec6f06813c8","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKGNjY2E5ODdkZTc4YjcwNTc3MDA2MTUxMTlmNDM4ZWM2ZjA2ODEzYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","sha":"126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f"}],"sha":"ccca987de78b7057700615119f438ec6f06813c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/ccca987de78b7057700615119f438ec6f06813c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/349b6f24957e3406e8935b5b01380df880b8164b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:56:26Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:56:26Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: play the weapon''s own inspect animation in the 3D viewer\n\nA skin reads as a thing you hold rather than a turntable exhibit when it\nmoves, and the clip for that is already in every weapon GLB — viewer3d has\nbeen parsing it for a year and only ever using it to freeze a pose.\n\nThe motion is applied to the CAMERA and the whole light rig rather than to\nthe weapon, which is exactly equivalent to turning the weapon under a fixed\nrig and is the only version available here: a weapon''s geometry is CPU-skinned\ninto a static mesh at mount (bakePose) and its skeleton then drives nothing,\nwhile its stickers, charm pivot, collision grid and game-space offsets are all\nworld-space and measured once. Turning `object` would leave every one of them\nbehind. The environment map turns with the lamps, so highlights and\nreflections sweep together. Rotation only — the clip''s translation is authored\nin viewmodel space and would carry the item out of an orthographic crop.\n\nClip choice is an explicit per-tree list (PRESENTATION.inspectClips) with no\ngeneric fallback, and each candidate must MEASURE as turning the body bone\nbefore it is accepted, so a model that matches nothing — or matches a\nsingle-key pose — stays exactly as static as it is today.\n\nThe bakes are protected three ways: a `still` viewer never builds a mixer, the\nmotion never touches the model or any world coordinate, and snapshot() puts\nthe rig back before it captures. The admin skin-test sweep goes through\nsnapshotModel, so it is covered by the first of those.\n\nAlso here:\n- transport (play/pause + scrub) in ViewerControls, on the touch layout too;\n  view mode only, since an editor must not move under a sticker being aimed\n- prefers-reduced-motion suppresses the animation AND the idle turntable\n- the clip REPLACES the turntable rather than joining it, so the per-frame\n  cost is a mixer evaluation and a few matrix ops, not a second moving part\n- ?perf=1 prints the chosen clip, the play head, the turn, and every clip the\n  GLB offered; ?inspectclip=<name> tries any one of them\n- a Motion switch in the dev HUD, and ViewerOpts.inspect:false for measurement\n  harnesses (tools/shadertest''s runViewer now pins its camera)\n\nNever seen running — there is no models mount here. TODO.md carries the three\nlive checks and the moving-parts follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f74c3b73d2c16445476be11d1851d76d5ee8de78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/f74c3b73d2c16445476be11d1851d76d5ee8de78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/349b6f24957e3406e8935b5b01380df880b8164b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/349b6f24957e3406e8935b5b01380df880b8164b","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKDM0OWI2ZjI0OTU3ZTM0MDZlODkzNWI1YjAxMzgwZGY4ODBiODE2NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","sha":"126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f"}],"sha":"349b6f24957e3406e8935b5b01380df880b8164b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/349b6f24957e3406e8935b5b01380df880b8164b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:51:40Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:51:40Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: browse skins by collection\n\nYou could filter stickers by capsule but not weapons by collection, so\n\"show me everything in the Bravo case\" was unanswerable. The faceting\nmachinery was already shipping — it was simply never populated for\nfinishes.\n\ncatalog.ts (still the ONE reader of cs2-lib):\n- `collectionOf` fills the existing `collection` facet from cs2-lib''s\n  `collectionName`. That is NOT the `categoryName` the attachment index\n  reads: categoryName is the capsule and is undefined on all 1,492\n  weapons, collectionName is the collection and is undefined on all\n  11,144 stickers. 1,455 of 1,456 weapon finishes carry one (M4A4 | Howl\n  is the exception, its collection was withdrawn with the skin).\n- Knives and gloves carry none at all, so they are read backwards off\n  each container''s `specialIds` — and only when exactly ONE collection\n  offers them. The classic knife pool is the special of eleven cases at\n  once, so naming one would be a fabrication; 312 melee and 72 glove\n  finishes stay uncollected on purpose. 102 knife and 22 glove entries\n  get a real answer.\n- Agents get the facet too (all 63), which grows a Collection dropdown on\n  their sheet out of one line.\n- `paintedListing` replaces three near-identical copies of the finish\n  projection, which the collection page would have made a fourth.\n- `getCollections` / `getCollection` — 94 sets in release order, each\n  with its member ids so ownership is a client-side intersection, its\n  best finish as art and rarity, and how you get it (case / souvenir /\n  drop) read backwards off the containers.\n\nArmory: a Collections section in its own rail group, two levels like\nWeapons. The index facets by source and searches by name; a collection\nlands on its own hero, its finishes rarity-first, and a progress bar on\nthe breadcrumb line saying how many of the set are already yours. Tiles\nyou own are ticked, on every catalog — not only inside a collection.\n\nsortModes: \"Collection\" joins the item sorts, with the uncollected pinned\nto the bottom in both directions and rarity as the tiebreak inside a set.\n\nVerified: npm run typecheck clean; tools/steam-sync-coverage.ts and\ntools/inspect-roundtrip.ts both still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"016ecccb686f8529f6daa4a9a609f5cc94c279a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/016ecccb686f8529f6daa4a9a609f5cc94c279a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7","node_id":"C_kwDOTbx4WNoAKGQzMzZjMmMyMDRkNGRhNTcxNTcwZGRhYTkwZGI1YWYwYThhOGY1Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commit/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","sha":"126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/126865e5ad43f1022cb3ee30e550d7ca43d12f0f"}],"sha":"d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/d336c2c204d4da571570ddaa90db5af0a8a8f5b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/commits/524d156a3225eee4f40f759b861ed31cb7899cff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:37:54Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:37:54Z","email":"luke@lukepolo.com","name":"Luke Policinski"},"message":"feature: public loadouts show their stickers, patches and charm\n\nGET /api/loadout/:steamId — the endpoint behind ?player= links and the\nprofile tab — selected only team/slot/item_id/skinned/wear/seed/stattrak/\nnametag. Every attachment was dropped, so visiting someone''s loadout showed\na bare gun where they had five stickers and a charm: the part of a loadout\npeople actually spend their time on. The two public paths disagreed about\nwhat a loadout even was, since copy-from has always cloned the attachments.\n\nBackend: widen the SELECT to i.stickers/i.patches/i.charm_id/i.charm_offset\n(plus the stattrak_count the row type already promised), run the rows\nthrough withAttachments + enrichAttachments like /api/inventory does, and\nstrip every row handle on the way out — item_instance_id stays null as\nbefore, and withoutInstanceHandle now nulls the `inst` inside each enriched\nsticker/patch/charm too. charm_offset is dropped entirely: its x/y/z/seed\nare already folded into `charm`, so nothing but that handle would survive.\nStill unauthenticated, by design.\n\nFrontend: focusAttachments falls back from the owned instance to the public\nloadout row, which is the whole of \"render attachments in viewer mode\" —\nthe 3D stage already took stickers/charm, it was just never handed any.\n\nCopy loadout: /loadout/copy-from had no UI at all. It gets a button in the\nviewer header, gated on being someone else''s non-empty loadout while signed\nin, behind a confirm that says it overwrites the matching slots of your own\nloadout first. Two defects it inherits (dropped charm_offset, the source\nuser''s dead `inst` ids) are written up in TODO.md rather than fixed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"658470f1e039d427e2b8be94ff6fc77f250f7793","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/trees/658470f1e039d427e2b8be94ff6fc77f250f7793"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukepolo/5stack-inventory-plugin/git/commits/524d156a3225eee4f40f759b861ed31cb7899cff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2066668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepolo","id":2066668,"login":"lukepolo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjY2Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepolo/starred{/owner}{/rep