,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/21221ed18fab35f4733af1cb164ab7b9803d5991/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:17:08Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:17:08Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"message":"Merge hardening/security-and-ml-review\n\nAddresses an external review of AgentShield (2 P0, 11 P1, 3 P2) covering\nmissing tests/CI, ML label leakage, weak split methodology, fail-open\nauthorization semantics, weak pseudonymization, hard-coded secrets,\noverstated benchmarks, and unbounded audit endpoints.\n\nInvestigating those confirmed all 15 and surfaced several more that only\nappeared once the system was run end to end -- three policy rules that\ncould never fire, a model that contributed nothing at runtime, and a\nconcurrency ceiling in a different component than assumed.\n\nThe repository had no tests and no CI. It now has 360 Go test cases at\n86.4% coverage, 81 Python tests, and GitHub Actions running all three\nsuites. The README documented a Makefile, compose stack, and Dockerfiles\nthat did not exist; those now exist and every documented command works\nfrom a clean clone.\n\nModel metrics changed substantially and deliberately: the served\nconfiguration reports 0.7659 accuracy / 0.8275 ROC-AUC against a 0.7614\nmajority-class floor, replacing a 0.9932 figure that depended on columns\nwhich are consequences of the access decision. The old number is retained\nonly as a labelled, non-servable upper bound.","tree":{"sha":"180210104ac03db2b1881d91e1660a2942be0588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/trees/180210104ac03db2b1881d91e1660a2942be0588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/commits/21221ed18fab35f4733af1cb164ab7b9803d5991","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/21221ed18fab35f4733af1cb164ab7b9803d5991","node_id":"C_kwDOTb8HFNoAKDIxMjIxZWQxOGZhYjM1ZjQ3MzNhZjFjYjE2NGFiN2I5ODAzZDU5OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/68657a72add4f1782d60ff66187b0faf531df20d","sha":"68657a72add4f1782d60ff66187b0faf531df20d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/68657a72add4f1782d60ff66187b0faf531df20d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe","sha":"b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe"}],"sha":"21221ed18fab35f4733af1cb164ab7b9803d5991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/21221ed18fab35f4733af1cb164ab7b9803d5991"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:52Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:52Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"message":"Replace unverifiable benchmark claims with measured numbers\n\nEvery benchmark in the README cited docs/resume_metrics.md, which has never\nexisted in git history, and no benchmark code backed the \"398K events/sec\"\ntable. The numbers also invited misreading: an in-memory hashing rate sat\ndirectly beside end-to-end HTTP latencies as though they measured the same\nthing.\n\nAll figures re-measured on a documented host with the conditions stated\nalongside each one:\n\n- Chain verification is labelled as in-memory recomputation with no\n  database or API I/O, and now reports the 174 MB it costs at 100K events.\n- Sequential and concurrent runs are separated, with the scoring-worker\n  count and chain depth given for each.\n- The concurrency ceiling is attributed correctly. The audit advisory lock\n  is genuinely serialized but sustains ~220-250 inserts/sec, roughly 5x the\n  end-to-end rate; the real limit was the single-worker scoring service,\n  where 20-wide concurrency was slower than sequential. Fixing it took\n  throughput from 16.3 to 41.0 req/s.\n- Model metrics report the served leakage-free configuration against the\n  majority-class floor, with the leaky number kept only as a labelled\n  upper bound.\n\nAdds docs/threat_model.md stating what the hash chain does not prove: an\nactor with database write access can rewrite history and recompute every\nsubsequent hash, and tail truncation is undetectable without an external\ncheckpoint. Also documents that no endpoint is authenticated.\n\nAdds docs/dataset_card.md covering provenance (undocumented origin,\nunknown licence), label construction, and the leakage analysis.","tree":{"sha":"180210104ac03db2b1881d91e1660a2942be0588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/trees/180210104ac03db2b1881d91e1660a2942be0588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/commits/b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe","node_id":"C_kwDOTb8HFNoAKGIzOTIwNDIwZDRjYzZmNTcxYjRhMjk2YmEyNWNhNjE2NmY2OGRjYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3","sha":"b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3"}],"sha":"b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/b3920420d4cc6f571b4a296ba25ca6166f68dcbe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:40Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:40Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"message":"Remove label leakage from the model and add group/OOD evaluation\n\nThe reported 0.9932 test accuracy came from label leakage.\npermission_match == 0 implies Blocked in 1337 of 1337 rows, and\nbuild_feature_artifacts kept every non-target column, so four fields that\nare consequences of the access decision went straight into the model. A\nthree-rule list over those same columns reaches 0.9409 with no learning.\n\nWorse, the model contributed nothing at runtime. The gateway sends tool and\nrole names absent from the training vocabulary, so handle_unknown=\"ignore\"\nzeroed roughly 60 of 69 features and the live score came entirely from four\nnumbers the service fabricated with keyword heuristics.\n\n- The served model excludes permission_match, human_approval_required,\n  action_risk_score, and data_exfiltration_risk. Honest metrics: 0.7659\n  accuracy, 0.8275 ROC-AUC, against a 0.7614 majority-class floor.\n- The fabricating heuristics are removed from the serving path and kept\n  only in baselines.py for comparison.\n- ablation.py and group_eval.py publish the evidence, including held-out\n  group performance. Held-out agent_role accuracy (0.7423) falls below the\n  majority floor -- reported as measured, not tuned away.\n- Out-of-vocabulary inputs are detected and reported so the gateway can\n  refuse to trust the score.\n- Artifacts carry model_version, dataset and schema hashes, and the\n  scikit-learn version; the service refuses to serve on a minor-version\n  mismatch rather than risk silently mis-scoring.\n- Explanations are no longer labelled as model signals: they are global\n  importance times active value, and say so.\n- The target column is pinned instead of inferred by keyword.\n\nThe simulator now uses the dataset taxonomy, generates timestamps inside\nthe gateway''s clock-skew window, and stamps them in send order so\nmulti-step sequences are coherent. The load generator sizes its own thread\npool so requested concurrency is achieved rather than nominal.\n\nAdds 81 tests. Removes the dead unsafe_label schema path and its scripts.","tree":{"sha":"7a3849b5646b08c389aeb446ac74642939d32471","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/trees/7a3849b5646b08c389aeb446ac74642939d32471"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/commits/b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3","node_id":"C_kwDOTb8HFNoAKGI3YzBmNDJlMmRhNGY5YmJmNmFhYzg3ZWRmYzI4YzM0ZTU2NjI3YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf","sha":"bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf"}],"sha":"b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/b7c0f42e2da4f9bbf6aac87edfc28c34e56627c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:26Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:26Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"message":"Fix fail-open authorization semantics and harden the gateway\n\nSecurity correctness:\n- PolicyResult.Allowed was `decision != deny`, making an escalation\n  technically \"allowed\". It is now `decision == allow`.\n- Unparseable resource_sensitivity ranked as medium; it now ranks at the\n  maximum so a typo escalates rather than silently downgrading.\n- On scorer failure the response was forced to deny but the original\n  PolicyResult was still persisted, so policy_decisions rows could record\n  \"allow\" under a denied event.\n- Three of six shipped policy rules keyed on vocabulary the system never\n  emits (tool: database_export, action: delete, agent_role:\n  autonomous_admin) and therefore never fired -- a 1000-action run produced\n  zero denies while appearing to enforce a contractor-exfiltration ban.\n  Rewritten against the real taxonomy, with a reachability test that fails\n  CI if a rule can no longer match.\n- resource_sensitivity accepted only a JSON string, rejecting the integer\n  form the dataset and ML service both use; this failed 1000/1000 requests.\n\nPrivacy and configuration:\n- HashIdentifier moves from salted SHA-256 to keyed HMAC-SHA256.\n- Config.Validate refuses to start in production with a default secret,\n  sslmode=disable, or the built-in credentials.\n\nProvenance and integrity:\n- Migration 0003 adds request_id, model_version, model_artifact_sha256,\n  policy_version, policy_sha256, gateway_version, decision_latency_ms, and\n  chain_schema_version. Version 1 records keep their original canonical\n  form and still verify, which is what makes this non-breaking.\n- Replay protection: repeated request_id returns the original decision and\n  writes no second event; timestamps outside the skew window are rejected.\n\nScale and operability:\n- Keyset pagination with asc/desc order on /v1/audit/events; chain\n  verification streams in batches at constant memory; attachPolicyDecisions\n  no longer scans the entire table.\n- /live and /ready alongside /health; readiness checks database, policy,\n  and model service.\n- Out-of-vocabulary scores can no longer produce an allow.\n\nModule path corrected to match the repository. Adds the first tests in the\nproject: 360 cases at 86.4% coverage, plus chain and insert benchmarks.","tree":{"sha":"2be776f922a4e27a7d1bd899e5b3adf95881997f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/trees/2be776f922a4e27a7d1bd899e5b3adf95881997f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/commits/bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf","node_id":"C_kwDOTb8HFNoAKGJlYTFlMjg3YmZhODFkOWZhYTQzMmU5NGI0YTU5ODcyNGU2MDUxY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commit/fae113061722bcc09249e832179c26ecfc69d544","sha":"fae113061722bcc09249e832179c26ecfc69d544","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/fae113061722bcc09249e832179c26ecfc69d544"}],"sha":"bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/bea1e287bfa81d9faa432e94b4a598724e6051cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/commits/fae113061722bcc09249e832179c26ecfc69d544/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:14Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:39:14Z","email":"maanavrajesh15@gmail.com","name":"MaanavR"},"message":"Add build, container, and CI infrastructure\n\nThe README documented a Makefile, docker-compose stack, and backend\nDockerfiles that did not exist, so every \"How To Run\" command failed on a\nfresh clone. There was also no .gitignore anywhere, leaving ~250 MB of\nnode_modules and build output one `git add -A` away from being committed.\n\nAdds .gitignore, .dockerignore, .env.example, a Makefile, a four-service\ncompose stack, distroless/slim Dockerfiles for the gateway and ML service,\nand GitHub Actions running the Go, Python, and frontend suites. The Go job\nruns against a postgres:16 service container so the integration tests\nexecute rather than skip.\n\nThe ML service runs multiple uvicorn workers: scoring is CPU-bound sklearn\ninference behind a synchronous endpoint, so a single worker serialized on\nthe GIL and capped the whole gateway.","tree":{"sha":"89089cc05d82d97c3c2c7b7d1aafb4a49a9aa344","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/trees/89089cc05d82d97c3c2c7b7d1aafb4a49a9aa344"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maanavrajesh/AgentShield/git/commits/fae113061722bcc09249e832179c26ecfc69d544","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139261689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maanavrajesh","id":139261689,"login":"maanavrajesh","node_id":"U_kgDOCEz2-Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maanavrajesh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maa