ps://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Suyashtripathi151/job-hunter-server/commits/1729741f14413a2f4c04e887a89c4e3d17846e14/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:33:28Z","email":"suyash@haltdos.com","name":"Suyash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:33:28Z","email":"suyash@haltdos.com","name":"Suyash"},"message":"Pre-create /data/resumes with app ownership in the image\n\nThe app container drops all capabilities (cap_drop: ALL), so it can''t\nchown the resumes_data volume itself once mounted. Docker copies this\npath''s content and ownership from the image into the volume on first\nuse (when the volume is empty), so creating it here as app:app is what\nmakes a fresh volume come up writable by the app user.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c9458d893ead2198686e7c7a6b55f068859396c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Suyashtripathi151/job-hunter-server/git/trees/4c9458d893ead2198686e7c7a6b55f068859396c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Suyashtripathi151/job-hunter-server/git/commits/1729741f14413a2f4c04e887a89c4e3d17846e14","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/156411003?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuyashHdos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","htm